WEBVTT

00:00:10.469 --> 00:00:13.139
[musical swirl]

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.647
[electric chimes]

00:00:29.572 --> 00:00:31.490
[orchestra tuning]

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:44.837
[soft music]

00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:03.355
[muffled sounds]

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.526
[music swells]

00:01:09.695 --> 00:01:11.572
[birds chirping]

00:01:18.662 --> 00:01:20.122
[soft snoring]

00:01:20.414 --> 00:01:23.000
[distant Indian
war whoops and gunfire]

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:27.838
[canon fire and yelling]

00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:34.887
[cannon fire booms]

00:01:36.806 --> 00:01:38.098
[cannon fire booms]

00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:43.020
[gasping]

00:01:47.942 --> 00:01:49.652
[cacophony of
gunfire and yelling]

00:01:52.613 --> 00:01:53.948
[horse neighs]

00:01:56.992 --> 00:01:59.578
Where is the General?
Where is he?

00:02:09.296 --> 00:02:10.881
Where is Braddock?

00:02:13.342 --> 00:02:14.343
[gun cocks]

00:02:15.678 --> 00:02:16.512
What happened?

00:02:16.637 --> 00:02:17.805
We've been ambushed!

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:18.597
From where?

00:02:18.764 --> 00:02:19.765
Over the hill!

00:02:29.275 --> 00:02:30.734
[panting]

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:32.945
[sounds muffle,
gasping as ringing starts]

00:02:34.238 --> 00:02:35.948
[grunts, sounds returning]

00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:42.830
[dramatic music]

00:02:49.086 --> 00:02:50.629
[cannon fire booms]

00:02:50.963 --> 00:02:52.590
[dramatic music intensifies]

00:02:58.804 --> 00:02:59.847
[coughing]

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:04.894
I wouldn't bother, Washington.

00:03:05.603 --> 00:03:06.812
The battle is lost.

00:03:06.937 --> 00:03:08.063
Where is the General?

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:09.398
Ordered a full retreat.

00:03:09.648 --> 00:03:11.609
That way lies nothing but death.

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:12.610
And my men?

00:03:14.153 --> 00:03:14.904
You have no men.

00:03:15.029 --> 00:03:16.238
The Virginians.

00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:19.700
They were at
the front of the line.

00:03:21.535 --> 00:03:23.954
If you go that way,
you will die.

00:03:24.663 --> 00:03:26.540
You look like death already.

00:03:26.665 --> 00:03:27.791
Listen to me.

00:03:30.127 --> 00:03:31.795
You'll never find them,
and even if you did,

00:03:31.921 --> 00:03:33.297
you'd never make it back.

00:03:33.797 --> 00:03:35.049
[cannon fire booms]

00:03:35.382 --> 00:03:36.175
Washington.

00:03:37.051 --> 00:03:38.135
Washington!

00:03:39.011 --> 00:03:40.137
Come, my friend.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.349
What could be worth the risk?

00:03:43.474 --> 00:03:45.559
[dramatic stinger]

00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:57.196
[solemn music]

00:04:05.204 --> 00:04:06.830
[solemn music continues]

00:04:21.303 --> 00:04:22.554
- [Lawrence] Mary.

00:04:23.013 --> 00:04:23.931
I'm so sorry.

00:04:25.933 --> 00:04:27.226
This must be Jack.

00:04:27.351 --> 00:04:29.728
This is... our Jack

00:04:29.895 --> 00:04:31.188
[Mary whispers to baby]

00:04:32.189 --> 00:04:33.315
Where is he?

00:04:34.191 --> 00:04:35.067
He's there.

00:04:35.609 --> 00:04:37.569
He’s not spoken since...

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:40.406
[Mary] since his father died.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.785
[solemn music continues]

00:04:54.503 --> 00:04:55.713
Hello, George.

00:05:04.847 --> 00:05:07.016
Do you remember me?

00:05:07.558 --> 00:05:09.226
I'm your half-brother.

00:05:09.685 --> 00:05:10.477
Lawrence.

00:05:12.104 --> 00:05:13.564
You're an officer?

00:05:13.856 --> 00:05:15.065
I was, yes.

00:05:16.525 --> 00:05:18.861
Captain in his Majesty's Navy.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.073
I have something for you.

00:05:27.536 --> 00:05:29.246
It’s a surveyor’s compass.

00:05:29.371 --> 00:05:32.082
It measures distances
of land and sea.

00:05:33.042 --> 00:05:34.626
This was our father's.

00:05:35.377 --> 00:05:36.754
And now it's yours.

00:05:37.129 --> 00:05:38.589
Won’t you need it?

00:05:39.798 --> 00:05:43.052
Well, my next adventure is
here with you, George.

00:05:44.428 --> 00:05:47.931
I have been appointed Adjutant
General of the Virginia militia.

00:05:48.182 --> 00:05:50.559
So, you will command soldiers?

00:05:50.684 --> 00:05:52.519
I'm to organize militia.

00:05:54.313 --> 00:05:55.439
Volunteers, really.

00:05:57.357 --> 00:05:59.735
[wagon wheels rumbling]

00:06:02.321 --> 00:06:03.947
[mournful music plays]

00:06:16.585 --> 00:06:19.213
[George] Do Washington
men die young?

00:06:19.338 --> 00:06:20.297
[Lawrence] What?

00:06:20.589 --> 00:06:23.425
[George] I heard them say
Washington men die young.

00:06:23.592 --> 00:06:25.761
That it's a curse to our name.

00:06:27.012 --> 00:06:28.013
Is that true?

00:06:30.808 --> 00:06:32.351
Are you afraid to die?

00:06:44.154 --> 00:06:47.116
[George] Mother says I will
not be going back to school.

00:06:47.241 --> 00:06:49.493
[Lawrence] There's nothing
wrong with tenant farming.

00:06:49.618 --> 00:06:50.953
It's an honorable profession.

00:06:51.078 --> 00:06:52.788
[George] But that is not
what I want.

00:06:53.247 --> 00:06:54.915
[Lawrence] It's what
duty demands.

00:06:55.457 --> 00:06:57.876
Time and circumstance
have changed.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:00.712
William Fairfax
is attending school.

00:07:00.963 --> 00:07:01.839
Why can I not?

00:07:02.131 --> 00:07:04.842
The Fairfaxes
are of a superior class.

00:07:05.384 --> 00:07:08.428
With advantages we
will never possess, George.

00:07:08.637 --> 00:07:11.265
The world is
often an unfair place.

00:07:12.599 --> 00:07:16.603
And you must take what
it gives you and make it yours.

00:07:16.812 --> 00:07:17.938
Now come inside.

00:07:20.023 --> 00:07:21.984
[bright music plays]

00:07:23.986 --> 00:07:25.737
George, where are you going?

00:07:25.863 --> 00:07:26.905
To school!

00:07:28.699 --> 00:07:30.325
Stubborn child.

00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:38.709
[Lawrence] It's two miles.

00:07:39.418 --> 00:07:40.210
I know.

00:07:41.587 --> 00:07:43.380
They will not let you in.

00:07:43.505 --> 00:07:44.590
[George] They will.

00:07:48.385 --> 00:07:50.053
[axe thuds]

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:53.974
Don't take it out on the tree.

00:07:54.266 --> 00:07:56.185
George. Stop, stop!

00:07:57.019 --> 00:07:57.936
[Mary sighs]

00:07:58.437 --> 00:08:00.814
They turned me away.
Because of you.

00:08:00.939 --> 00:08:02.566
And now I have nothing.

00:08:03.567 --> 00:08:04.443
Nothing?

00:08:04.568 --> 00:08:05.402
[scoffs]

00:08:05.694 --> 00:08:08.906
We have 250 acres.

00:08:09.031 --> 00:08:11.783
Ten slaves in bondage
to feed.

00:08:11.909 --> 00:08:14.536
And one widow's purse,
near empty.

00:08:15.621 --> 00:08:17.706
You're the eldest son
in this house,

00:08:17.831 --> 00:08:19.499
and you have
a duty to it.

00:08:19.625 --> 00:08:21.919
That is not what I want.
I want more than this.

00:08:22.085 --> 00:08:24.922
And I want a husband,
back from his fever.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:26.757
Providence denied me this.

00:08:26.882 --> 00:08:28.675
Then Providence is cruel!

00:08:32.387 --> 00:08:35.974
God raises
what is well grounded.

00:08:37.726 --> 00:08:40.520
You'll not abandon
what is yours, nor will I.

00:08:40.979 --> 00:08:42.397
You're my son,

00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:46.485
and a Washington,
and you'll behave like both.

00:08:48.487 --> 00:08:50.030
[Mary sighs deeply]

00:08:52.908 --> 00:08:53.784
[sighs]

00:08:56.787 --> 00:08:58.330
[door creaks open]

00:09:09.675 --> 00:09:11.510
[Lawrence breathes deeply]

00:09:20.686 --> 00:09:21.353
Here.

00:09:22.437 --> 00:09:25.274
Rules of Civility
and Decent Behavior.

00:09:25.399 --> 00:09:28.610
That will teach you
how to be a proper gentleman.

00:09:28.777 --> 00:09:32.739
Then Cato. Plutarch.
Essential readings.

00:09:33.949 --> 00:09:35.659
Seneca and Cincinnatus.

00:09:36.702 --> 00:09:40.872
If one desires to be great,
he must study those that were.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.042
It’s a lot of books, I know--

00:09:46.586 --> 00:09:49.381
I am sorry for
your misfortune, George.

00:09:50.549 --> 00:09:54.970
If no one else will
teach you, I'll teach you.

00:09:56.054 --> 00:09:57.848
But I could loan you these,

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:00.058
one by one,

00:10:02.185 --> 00:10:03.770
if you do your chores.

00:10:05.689 --> 00:10:07.274
[bright music]

00:10:08.775 --> 00:10:11.361
[Lawrence] “Every public
action should” what?

00:10:11.486 --> 00:10:13.739
[George] “Show respect to
those who are present.”

00:10:13.864 --> 00:10:15.699
What do you
think respect means?

00:10:15.824 --> 00:10:19.494
[George] To listen to or obey
the one you are respecting.

00:10:20.162 --> 00:10:21.079
[Lawrence] Perhaps.

00:10:21.913 --> 00:10:24.124
But obedience can be commanded.

00:10:24.833 --> 00:10:26.585
Respect must be earned.

00:10:28.086 --> 00:10:30.422
That is why I became a soldier.

00:10:30.547 --> 00:10:32.758
[bright music continues]

00:10:33.967 --> 00:10:36.803
Aristocracy is a game, George.

00:10:36.928 --> 00:10:39.723
But, you could learn
to play it, I suppose.

00:10:39.848 --> 00:10:41.224
What piece are we?

00:10:41.808 --> 00:10:43.310
We are pawns, George.

00:10:45.979 --> 00:10:48.273
But even a pawn can take a king.

00:10:49.274 --> 00:10:50.317
Play again?

00:10:51.193 --> 00:10:52.069
Yeah.

00:10:52.778 --> 00:10:53.487
Up.

00:10:55.781 --> 00:10:57.240
[Lawrence] Very nice, George.

00:10:58.158 --> 00:11:00.369
[Lawrence] Remember, heels down,
chest up.

00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:03.538
I think it's
now time you ride alone.

00:11:04.289 --> 00:11:05.457
Wouldn't you agree?

00:11:05.582 --> 00:11:06.249
Yes.

00:11:06.375 --> 00:11:07.292
Very well.

00:11:07.417 --> 00:11:08.210
Go on then.

00:11:08.794 --> 00:11:10.587
[adventurous music]

00:11:11.046 --> 00:11:12.297
[Lawrence] Not too fast now.

00:11:13.507 --> 00:11:14.758
Steady.

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:19.471
[young George] “To obtain
the applause of

00:11:19.596 --> 00:11:23.517
deserving men
is a heartfelt satisfaction...”

00:11:26.686 --> 00:11:28.605
[adventurous music swells]

00:11:28.730 --> 00:11:32.984
[George] “...to merit them
is my highest wish...”

00:11:44.121 --> 00:11:45.997
[indistinct chatter]

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:49.751
[Col. Gooch] So, here he is.

00:11:49.876 --> 00:11:52.337
The boy who
writes all the letters...

00:11:52.462 --> 00:11:54.506
petitioning for a
‘royal’ commission?

00:11:54.631 --> 00:11:55.298
Yes, sir.

00:11:55.882 --> 00:11:57.717
I dream of
becoming a British officer.

00:11:57.884 --> 00:12:00.637
Ensign or lieutenant,
as his Majesty sees fit.

00:12:01.513 --> 00:12:03.974
I believe my brother
communicated this on my behalf.

00:12:04.391 --> 00:12:05.684
Lawrence Washington.

00:12:05.809 --> 00:12:07.144
He served under the--

00:12:07.269 --> 00:12:09.896
If I were to allow it...
the purchase price

00:12:10.021 --> 00:12:13.108
for an ensigncy in the
Coldstreams is £700.

00:12:13.233 --> 00:12:14.568
Do you possess that, sir?

00:12:14.734 --> 00:12:15.944
No, sir. I do not.

00:12:16.069 --> 00:12:18.029
Then why not
seek to join the militia?

00:12:18.155 --> 00:12:20.782
Well, I wish to serve
the Crown as an actual officer.

00:12:20.907 --> 00:12:23.368
Then how much
land do you possess?

00:12:23.535 --> 00:12:26.204
I am a custodian, um,
under my brother's estate

00:12:26.329 --> 00:12:27.247
at Mount Vernon.

00:12:27.372 --> 00:12:28.373
Tenant farmer.

00:12:29.207 --> 00:12:30.250
Education?

00:12:30.417 --> 00:12:33.920
I received no formal schooling
after my father died, sir.

00:12:34.045 --> 00:12:36.006
But I recently obtained
my surveyor's license.

00:12:36.131 --> 00:12:37.799
To be a British officer,

00:12:38.049 --> 00:12:40.177
you must first be a gentleman.

00:12:40.469 --> 00:12:43.096
If I may, sir, how is it that my
brother qualified yet I do not?

00:12:43.221 --> 00:12:44.473
He owns Mount Vernon.

00:12:44.598 --> 00:12:47.142
He was properly
educated in England.

00:12:47.267 --> 00:12:48.894
And what's more,
he's married to a Fairfax.

00:12:49.019 --> 00:12:51.438
Yes, and he has
been a great mentor to me.

00:12:51.563 --> 00:12:53.732
I-I've studied
to become a gentleman.

00:12:53.857 --> 00:12:55.817
I've even compiled
all I've learned.

00:12:55.984 --> 00:12:58.653
Goodness, man,
how much do you write?

00:12:58.945 --> 00:13:00.322
Well, I've compiled
it from other books.

00:13:00.447 --> 00:13:02.199
It's called Rules of
Civility and Decent Behaviour.

00:13:02.324 --> 00:13:04.242
Which is to say
you plagiarised it.

00:13:04.367 --> 00:13:05.160
No. No, no--

00:13:05.869 --> 00:13:07.078
Well, yes, but, err...

00:13:08.038 --> 00:13:11.249
Imitation of great men
does not make you one.

00:13:15.587 --> 00:13:16.463
I... I ask again, sir.

00:13:16.588 --> 00:13:18.381
How may I become a
British officer of the Crown?

00:13:18.507 --> 00:13:19.841
- You cannot--
- There must be a path.

00:13:19.966 --> 00:13:22.552
There is not for you.

00:13:23.929 --> 00:13:27.098
And please,
stop writing me letters.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:34.648
Go!

00:13:35.398 --> 00:13:36.691
[dramatic music]

00:14:06.304 --> 00:14:07.389
[George] Hello, Jack.

00:14:09.224 --> 00:14:10.475
Good to see you.

00:14:12.018 --> 00:14:13.645
Are you an officer now?

00:14:14.437 --> 00:14:15.105
Not yet.

00:14:16.189 --> 00:14:16.940
But someday.

00:14:17.649 --> 00:14:18.608
[Mary] Or never.

00:14:20.193 --> 00:14:22.112
If God hears my prayers.

00:14:35.917 --> 00:14:37.460
“Be not tedious in discourse.”

00:14:37.877 --> 00:14:39.129
[exhales]

00:14:39.254 --> 00:14:40.630
Especially tonight.

00:14:42.007 --> 00:14:43.383
[distant footfalls]

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.388
Where are you off to?

00:14:50.307 --> 00:14:51.433
To see Lawrence.

00:14:52.058 --> 00:14:56.146
At Belvoir? You're not invited.
How do you expect to get in?

00:14:56.271 --> 00:14:58.273
Is it a sin to seek advancement?

00:14:58.398 --> 00:14:59.399
It is to them.

00:15:01.151 --> 00:15:02.611
You're just a pawn to them.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:08.158
Well, even a pawn
can take a king.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.663
[noble fanfare]

00:15:14.039 --> 00:15:15.498
[classical music plays]

00:15:25.467 --> 00:15:26.468
[Steward] Invitation, sir.

00:15:26.593 --> 00:15:29.929
I am Mr. Washington, uh,
George Washington.

00:15:30.805 --> 00:15:32.140
Half-brother to Lawrence,

00:15:32.265 --> 00:15:35.185
who is married to Anne,
formerly Fairfax.

00:15:35.644 --> 00:15:39.522
Thank you for the genealogy.
Now, your invitation, sir?

00:15:39.648 --> 00:15:40.315
Ah.

00:15:41.691 --> 00:15:43.068
Um... I don't have it.

00:15:44.402 --> 00:15:46.071
The guests for this party
have been chosen

00:15:46.196 --> 00:15:49.407
with great specificity,
so I suggest you find it.

00:15:49.532 --> 00:15:50.617
Mr. Washington.

00:15:52.035 --> 00:15:52.702
Sir.

00:15:54.287 --> 00:15:55.288
Ah...

00:15:55.747 --> 00:15:56.915
- Good evening.
- Thank you.

00:16:00.877 --> 00:16:03.630
[curious music]

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.931
[laughter]

00:16:32.659 --> 00:16:33.493
Good evening.

00:16:33.618 --> 00:16:34.327
- Good evening.
- Evening, sir.

00:16:34.452 --> 00:16:35.870
We need more ice.

00:16:37.122 --> 00:16:38.581
Uh, can I, can I carry
that upstairs?

00:16:38.707 --> 00:16:39.874
Uh, no need, sir.

00:16:43.712 --> 00:16:45.588
How-how do I get in
the house?

00:16:47.549 --> 00:16:49.551
[string music plays]

00:17:07.944 --> 00:17:09.320
[woman] You don't
belong here.

00:17:12.073 --> 00:17:13.992
Clever entrance, though.

00:17:14.951 --> 00:17:17.203
Most guests just
enter through the front door.

00:17:17.328 --> 00:17:19.831
My brother spoke to
me of this gathering. He is--

00:17:19.956 --> 00:17:21.583
Married to Ann Fairfax.

00:17:22.208 --> 00:17:23.334
Yes, I know.

00:17:24.502 --> 00:17:26.796
You, on the
other hand, are not.

00:17:27.255 --> 00:17:28.798
A child of one of Virginia's

00:17:28.923 --> 00:17:31.384
largest fortunes and
family estates?

00:17:31.509 --> 00:17:33.094
You're right. I'm not.

00:17:33.803 --> 00:17:35.805
And you were right. I'm rich.

00:17:36.514 --> 00:17:37.515
But...

00:17:37.682 --> 00:17:39.350
I also don't feel
like I belong.

00:17:39.476 --> 00:17:42.312
Well, that's like saying a rose
doesn't belong in a garden.

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:47.066
I'll take that compliment.

00:17:47.317 --> 00:17:49.819
I'd be happy
if there were more.

00:17:51.529 --> 00:17:55.325
Here's the problem with
trying to sneak into a party.

00:17:55.533 --> 00:17:58.912
You, sir, stand out in a crowd.

00:18:01.164 --> 00:18:02.540
Then dance with me.

00:18:02.749 --> 00:18:05.126
I only dance
with invited guests.

00:18:05.585 --> 00:18:08.838
Well, perhaps you should make
room for someone truly worthy.

00:18:08.963 --> 00:18:12.050
Because, I don’t see anyone
like that here.

00:18:12.967 --> 00:18:16.304
Mr. Washington, aren't you bold?

00:18:19.349 --> 00:18:20.350
Well, I'm off.

00:18:20.475 --> 00:18:21.184
To where?

00:18:23.019 --> 00:18:25.188
To fulfill my solemn duty.

00:18:27.649 --> 00:18:28.650
Charm.

00:18:33.071 --> 00:18:35.490
[Lawrence] Gently does it,
George.

00:18:36.282 --> 00:18:38.660
Best to proceed with caution.

00:18:39.035 --> 00:18:41.037
It would profit Sally's
family greatly

00:18:41.162 --> 00:18:43.581
if she were to
marry a Fairfax.

00:18:43.706 --> 00:18:44.916
Like you did?

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:46.876
[Lawrence chuckles]

00:18:47.627 --> 00:18:48.336
Yes.

00:18:49.629 --> 00:18:53.216
And until I did, I held all my
hopes very loosely.

00:18:54.634 --> 00:18:56.803
The odds were against me.

00:18:59.347 --> 00:19:02.433
Well, the odds
have always been against us.

00:19:02.559 --> 00:19:03.476
Wish me luck.

00:19:05.019 --> 00:19:05.728
Good luck.

00:19:08.731 --> 00:19:10.316
[indistinct conversation]

00:19:12.235 --> 00:19:15.196
William. Thank you for
having me in your home.

00:19:15.321 --> 00:19:17.156
George, what a surprise.

00:19:17.907 --> 00:19:20.535
I didn't expect to
see you in a place like this.

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:22.120
How ever did you get in?

00:19:22.245 --> 00:19:25.415
I was enticed by the
promise of beautiful women.

00:19:25.540 --> 00:19:27.417
Well, we'd
hate to disappoint you.

00:19:27.542 --> 00:19:28.585
You haven't.

00:19:29.586 --> 00:19:31.045
Meet Thomas Gage.

00:19:31.254 --> 00:19:34.674
Newly minted Major,
recently arrived from London

00:19:34.799 --> 00:19:36.050
by order of the Crown.

00:19:37.093 --> 00:19:37.760
Pleasure.

00:19:37.886 --> 00:19:38.595
Pleasure is mine.

00:19:39.095 --> 00:19:40.972
I, too, one day
hope to serve His Majesty.

00:19:41.222 --> 00:19:43.975
Tell me, Washington,
what is your opinion

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:46.895
of the French
building forts on our land?

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:49.647
Well, I think the Ohio
is a frontier.

00:19:49.772 --> 00:19:51.357
It belongs to the one
who tames it.

00:19:51.482 --> 00:19:52.609
- [William] Ah.
- Well said.

00:19:53.359 --> 00:19:57.822
But in reality, it belongs to
the one who buys it.

00:19:58.448 --> 00:20:00.199
That is the way
of things, is it not?

00:20:00.325 --> 00:20:01.659
[a minuet begins to play]

00:20:02.035 --> 00:20:05.997
Ah, a minuet.
I love a minuet.

00:20:06.789 --> 00:20:10.668
I believe I have the first
dance, if you'll excuse us.

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:17.967
Pleasure to meet you.
I hope we meet again.

00:20:18.092 --> 00:20:18.968
Pleasure.

00:20:23.306 --> 00:20:24.807
- Where are you off to?
- Sally.

00:20:25.058 --> 00:20:26.434
My solemn duty.

00:20:36.277 --> 00:20:37.695
[deep sigh]

00:20:43.242 --> 00:20:44.202
Ah!

00:20:46.162 --> 00:20:48.122
Lord Fairfax.
Begging your pardon.

00:20:48.831 --> 00:20:51.417
I've dreamed of
seeing your library.

00:20:53.336 --> 00:20:55.213
These are my true tenants.

00:20:57.340 --> 00:20:58.383
Who are you?

00:20:58.508 --> 00:21:01.219
George Washington, sir.
Brother to Lawrence.

00:21:01.344 --> 00:21:02.929
I didn't know he'd invited you.

00:21:03.054 --> 00:21:04.722
Neither did he,
if you must know.

00:21:04.847 --> 00:21:08.685
Ah! So, I've caught
you slipping in.

00:21:08.935 --> 00:21:10.103
And you...

00:21:10.728 --> 00:21:12.814
caught me slipping out. Come.

00:21:14.148 --> 00:21:15.608
I can't take much
of these soirées.

00:21:15.733 --> 00:21:17.360
So, I hide.

00:21:18.361 --> 00:21:21.698
Until my wife finds me
and rousts me back out.

00:21:23.199 --> 00:21:26.703
"When vice prevails, and
impious men bear sway,

00:21:26.828 --> 00:21:29.706
the post of
honor is a private station."

00:21:29.872 --> 00:21:30.832
Cato.

00:21:31.416 --> 00:21:32.417
You've seen the play?

00:21:32.542 --> 00:21:34.919
No, but I've read it
50 times over.

00:21:35.044 --> 00:21:37.296
"Tis not in mortals
to command success.

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:39.757
But we'll do more.
We'll deserve it."

00:21:39.966 --> 00:21:41.342
Well said. [chuckles]

00:21:42.093 --> 00:21:44.595
Do you happen to
have Pope's Essay on Man?

00:21:44.721 --> 00:21:46.639
Would it be imposing if I
asked to borrow it?

00:21:47.432 --> 00:21:49.642
I obtained a letter of
introduction from your cousin.

00:21:50.685 --> 00:21:52.812
An eccentric fellow, isn't he?

00:21:53.354 --> 00:21:54.272
Indeed he is.

00:21:54.939 --> 00:21:57.442
He lent me a book on surveying
from his library.

00:21:57.567 --> 00:21:59.360
Not nearly as grand as yours.

00:21:59.485 --> 00:22:01.696
I put it to good use
and obtained my license.

00:22:01.821 --> 00:22:03.823
I know you own
five million acres now.

00:22:04.449 --> 00:22:06.492
The only thing
a landowner ever desires...

00:22:08.327 --> 00:22:10.038
is the plot next to his.

00:22:11.789 --> 00:22:12.498
Yes, I do.

00:22:13.833 --> 00:22:16.502
I also know a
great amount of that land

00:22:16.627 --> 00:22:20.089
is in the Ohio Valley
and has not been charted.

00:22:20.423 --> 00:22:23.843
I sense a looming storm
over the Ohio Territory.

00:22:25.470 --> 00:22:26.596
Inevitable, I'm afraid.

00:22:26.971 --> 00:22:28.389
I could go there.

00:22:28.514 --> 00:22:30.600
Survey it and map it for you.

00:22:30.933 --> 00:22:32.226
A land that isn't
properly measured

00:22:32.351 --> 00:22:33.561
cannot be properly valued,

00:22:33.686 --> 00:22:34.854
or protected.

00:22:34.979 --> 00:22:36.981
Much of that
territory is unexplored.

00:22:37.106 --> 00:22:39.192
Many have traveled there,
never to be seen again.

00:22:39.317 --> 00:22:39.984
Yes.

00:22:41.152 --> 00:22:43.446
But no man who
lived a life of ease

00:22:43.571 --> 00:22:46.324
ever left a name
worth remembering, sir.

00:22:46.449 --> 00:22:48.117
I'll take the risk upon myself.

00:22:48.242 --> 00:22:49.118
I'll make it to the furthest

00:22:49.243 --> 00:22:51.537
reaches of your
plot and report back.

00:22:51.662 --> 00:22:53.706
And I'll put my name
to that promise.

00:22:53.831 --> 00:22:56.042
Is this man bothering you, sir?

00:23:00.588 --> 00:23:01.255
Hardly.

00:23:02.215 --> 00:23:04.425
I accept your proposal, George.

00:23:04.801 --> 00:23:05.885
Thank you, sir.

00:23:06.969 --> 00:23:08.971
[spirited, upbeat music]

00:23:13.226 --> 00:23:15.228
Enjoy the party, Washington.

00:23:18.106 --> 00:23:20.191
[indistinct chatter]

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:25.488
[man] Get out of the way.

00:23:32.537 --> 00:23:33.746
Christopher Gist.

00:23:35.665 --> 00:23:36.582
George?

00:23:37.542 --> 00:23:38.209
George.

00:23:42.213 --> 00:23:43.047
Good to see you.

00:23:43.172 --> 00:23:44.298
It's good to see you.

00:23:44.841 --> 00:23:48.344
George, these are the brothers
Frisk. Henry, the oldest,

00:23:48.636 --> 00:23:50.638
And his baby brother, David.

00:23:50.972 --> 00:23:52.807
[Christopher] My two
most loyal friends.

00:23:53.808 --> 00:23:54.475
Do not trust them.

00:23:54.600 --> 00:23:55.810
[laughs]

00:23:56.144 --> 00:23:57.770
That's a nice coat
you got there.

00:23:57.937 --> 00:23:59.438
Careful! He's a thief!

00:23:59.564 --> 00:24:00.314
Shut your--

00:24:00.439 --> 00:24:01.691
Leave him alone!

00:24:03.234 --> 00:24:05.611
Where are you
coming from, all...

00:24:06.112 --> 00:24:07.405
fresh and plucked?

00:24:09.448 --> 00:24:10.116
Belvoir.

00:24:10.491 --> 00:24:12.243
[mockingly] Ooh!

00:24:13.161 --> 00:24:16.747
That mean you too fancy to, uh,
place a little wager?

00:24:21.169 --> 00:24:22.461
How bout you place one for me?

00:24:22.587 --> 00:24:23.421
[laughs]

00:24:23.546 --> 00:24:25.423
Oh, I like him.

00:24:25.548 --> 00:24:26.924
What are you doing here?

00:24:27.049 --> 00:24:28.467
I have a job for us.

00:24:28.759 --> 00:24:30.386
I'm too drunk for work.

00:24:30.553 --> 00:24:32.889
Ambition waits for no man.

00:24:33.097 --> 00:24:33.890
What is it?

00:24:34.098 --> 00:24:36.267
Surveying the Ohio territory.

00:24:36.392 --> 00:24:38.269
I need someone who can
keep me alive.

00:24:39.228 --> 00:24:39.896
For who?

00:24:40.313 --> 00:24:41.230
Lord Fairfax.

00:24:43.482 --> 00:24:44.567
What part?

00:24:44.692 --> 00:24:45.902
Most all of it.

00:24:46.235 --> 00:24:47.486
He pays by the acre.

00:24:48.404 --> 00:24:49.405
[Henry laughs]

00:24:53.075 --> 00:24:54.118
Well...

00:24:55.119 --> 00:24:56.412
let's get it done.

00:24:56.621 --> 00:24:57.580
[laughs]

00:24:58.372 --> 00:24:59.248
To Virginia!

00:24:59.874 --> 00:25:00.750
To Virginia!

00:25:02.335 --> 00:25:04.420
[spirited, upbeat
music continues]

00:25:04.545 --> 00:25:06.923
That is the last time,
Henry!

00:25:07.173 --> 00:25:07.840
David!

00:25:08.174 --> 00:25:09.217
[incoherent yelling]

00:25:09.342 --> 00:25:10.968
She's your mother, too!

00:25:11.594 --> 00:25:13.262
Yeah, we don't
know that for sure.

00:25:13.512 --> 00:25:14.430
[men yelling fades out]

00:25:16.057 --> 00:25:19.143
[adventurous music]

00:25:21.020 --> 00:25:22.480
[George] It's beautiful,
isn't it?

00:25:23.147 --> 00:25:23.814
Yeah.

00:25:27.151 --> 00:25:29.070
But it don't belong to you.

00:25:29.695 --> 00:25:33.616
Well, if we go far enough,
it doesn't belong to anyone.

00:25:38.955 --> 00:25:40.206
[George] Dear madam,

00:25:40.706 --> 00:25:44.293
Gazing at the new world,
I now write to express my joy.

00:25:44.835 --> 00:25:45.795
I was honored with
your short

00:25:46.003 --> 00:25:49.632
but very agreeable favor
of our first acquaintance.

00:25:50.758 --> 00:25:51.717
In this case,

00:25:51.842 --> 00:25:54.637
the one who is too sensible of
her charms to deny the power,

00:25:54.762 --> 00:25:57.390
whose influence I feel
and must ever submit to.

00:25:57.848 --> 00:26:00.434
I am aware of
how impossible this is. But...

00:26:00.768 --> 00:26:02.144
if you will allow me
to prove myself,

00:26:02.311 --> 00:26:04.605
I pledge to rule out
all disappointment.

00:26:09.402 --> 00:26:12.154
I wish I could be with you.
Or rather, you here with me.

00:26:12.488 --> 00:26:16.075
So you could witness the
beauty of this land.

00:26:17.493 --> 00:26:18.828
Let's see who this is.

00:26:18.953 --> 00:26:20.538
Pass it-- pass it back.
Pass it back.

00:26:20.663 --> 00:26:22.415
Miss Sally Cary?

00:26:25.543 --> 00:26:28.587
You might as well petition the
Queen of England, George.

00:26:28.713 --> 00:26:30.506
She's above your station.

00:26:31.090 --> 00:26:31.966
Permanently.

00:26:34.010 --> 00:26:36.721
Fight battles you can win,
George.

00:26:38.389 --> 00:26:39.849
Nice signature, though.

00:26:41.142 --> 00:26:44.061
“I am your humble
devoted servant”.

00:26:46.397 --> 00:26:47.523
[rushing water]

00:26:55.906 --> 00:26:57.199
[horse neighing]

00:26:58.951 --> 00:27:00.745
[Christopher] We're not
going to make it back

00:27:00.953 --> 00:27:02.455
before winter sets in.

00:27:02.997 --> 00:27:04.749
[George] The horses
have done all they can.

00:27:05.583 --> 00:27:06.959
We must leave them.

00:27:07.710 --> 00:27:09.086
There’s a village,

00:27:09.253 --> 00:27:12.048
about a half a day’s
journey from here.

00:27:12.798 --> 00:27:14.008
We could shelter.

00:27:14.550 --> 00:27:15.301
Ride out the cold.

00:27:15.426 --> 00:27:17.053
No, no, that's too long a time.

00:27:17.178 --> 00:27:19.722
[shivering] I suppose you'd
rather freeze to death.

00:27:21.140 --> 00:27:22.475
We have to return.

00:27:23.017 --> 00:27:24.101
So you can see your
woman?

00:27:24.352 --> 00:27:25.728
So we can get paid.

00:27:26.729 --> 00:27:30.232
It’s unbecoming of a gentleman
to lie to himself.

00:27:31.484 --> 00:27:32.443
[whistles]

00:27:35.821 --> 00:27:37.740
[ominous music]

00:27:42.870 --> 00:27:44.997
[Christopher speaks Seneca]

00:27:51.253 --> 00:27:52.963
[speaking Seneca]

00:27:57.051 --> 00:27:59.470
He's not too
fond of your compass.

00:28:01.138 --> 00:28:02.390
Offer them the horses.

00:28:02.515 --> 00:28:03.307
George?

00:28:03.432 --> 00:28:05.059
They’re no longer
of use to us...

00:28:05.184 --> 00:28:07.728
but they could still be
saved to serve them.

00:28:07.853 --> 00:28:09.480
You offer dying horses?

00:28:11.565 --> 00:28:14.276
For the land
given to me by my father?

00:28:15.778 --> 00:28:17.113
To him by his father?

00:28:17.238 --> 00:28:18.614
Hey... hey.

00:28:20.449 --> 00:28:24.120
You have no right to take
what we possess for generations.

00:28:24.245 --> 00:28:26.747
We are not here
to claim this land.

00:28:29.542 --> 00:28:31.127
We are surveyors only.

00:28:53.858 --> 00:28:56.235
I know what
you want, Englishman.

00:28:57.319 --> 00:28:58.696
And I offer something
more.

00:29:02.533 --> 00:29:04.243
Something for your king.

00:29:10.791 --> 00:29:12.543
[dramatic music]

00:29:23.304 --> 00:29:24.555
Whose fort is that?

00:29:26.515 --> 00:29:27.641
The French.

00:29:32.146 --> 00:29:34.023
[dramatic music continues]

00:29:36.901 --> 00:29:38.194
[Christopher] Are you
sure

00:29:38.319 --> 00:29:40.154
this is the fastest way home?

00:29:40.988 --> 00:29:42.323
[George] Saves us two days.

00:29:42.448 --> 00:29:43.824
[Christopher] If we fall off
this raft,

00:29:43.949 --> 00:29:45.242
we'll freeze to death.

00:29:45.367 --> 00:29:46.952
No, no. We have to get
this information back.

00:29:48.120 --> 00:29:48.787
[grunts]

00:29:48.913 --> 00:29:50.998
You're full of
surprises, you know.

00:29:51.123 --> 00:29:52.416
Speaking their tongue?

00:29:53.125 --> 00:29:54.835
Well...”know thy enemy.”

00:29:55.211 --> 00:29:56.587
Are they the enemy?

00:29:56.837 --> 00:29:57.922
They let us go.

00:29:58.255 --> 00:30:00.382
Only because they hate
the French more than--

00:30:00.508 --> 00:30:02.218
More than they hate us.

00:30:05.638 --> 00:30:06.305
George.

00:30:06.430 --> 00:30:07.556
George, look!

00:30:07.806 --> 00:30:08.807
Look, look.

00:30:16.065 --> 00:30:17.066
Get to the shore!

00:30:17.191 --> 00:30:18.442
[both grunt with effort]

00:30:19.276 --> 00:30:19.985
Push!

00:30:20.194 --> 00:30:20.903
I'm trying.

00:30:21.028 --> 00:30:21.737
Get to the shore!

00:30:21.904 --> 00:30:23.614
The current is too strong.

00:30:25.741 --> 00:30:26.534
No.

00:30:28.869 --> 00:30:29.870
Christopher...

00:30:30.079 --> 00:30:31.038
Hold on, hold on.

00:30:31.163 --> 00:30:32.540
[both yell]

00:30:33.958 --> 00:30:35.251
[music intensifies]

00:30:36.168 --> 00:30:37.336
[gasps]

00:30:46.220 --> 00:30:47.221
[George] Swim!

00:30:48.430 --> 00:30:49.306
[Christopher] The maps!

00:30:49.598 --> 00:30:50.891
[George] Christopher!

00:30:51.100 --> 00:30:54.061
[dramatic music]

00:30:58.065 --> 00:30:59.191
Did you get the maps?

00:31:00.609 --> 00:31:02.111
[grunts]

00:31:14.331 --> 00:31:15.624
[grunts]

00:31:15.749 --> 00:31:16.792
[both shivering]

00:31:17.209 --> 00:31:20.087
George, you think
you could swim across?

00:31:22.047 --> 00:31:23.299
[grunts]

00:31:28.554 --> 00:31:30.264
Stay awake, George.

00:31:35.561 --> 00:31:37.104
Save your strength.

00:31:56.332 --> 00:31:57.207
Christopher.

00:31:59.418 --> 00:32:00.669
Christopher, wake up.

00:32:00.794 --> 00:32:01.462
Wake up!

00:32:02.546 --> 00:32:03.422
Christopher!

00:32:05.466 --> 00:32:07.134
[Christopher breathes
raggedly]

00:32:09.511 --> 00:32:11.221
You believe in miracles?

00:32:18.020 --> 00:32:18.729
Get up.

00:32:18.854 --> 00:32:20.147
How did it freeze?

00:32:23.150 --> 00:32:24.985
Do we risk it?

00:32:34.244 --> 00:32:35.829
[gasps]

00:32:44.546 --> 00:32:46.006
[Lawrence coughs]

00:32:51.178 --> 00:32:52.680
You can confirm this?

00:32:53.722 --> 00:32:54.390
Yes.

00:32:54.973 --> 00:32:56.809
So can Christopher Gist.

00:32:57.142 --> 00:32:58.143
[coughs]

00:32:59.228 --> 00:33:03.023
If you have these delivered to
Governor Dinwiddie, he can...

00:33:06.193 --> 00:33:07.319
Consumption.

00:33:08.570 --> 00:33:09.279
They say.

00:33:09.697 --> 00:33:10.864
[Lawrence coughs]

00:33:15.661 --> 00:33:17.413
All men die, George.

00:33:18.414 --> 00:33:20.416
I can't go to the governor
in my state.

00:33:21.583 --> 00:33:22.793
[coughs]

00:33:23.502 --> 00:33:25.879
You wish to
advance your station?

00:33:27.256 --> 00:33:29.550
My condition
may be your answer.

00:33:29.675 --> 00:33:31.552
[coughs]

00:33:37.015 --> 00:33:38.559
[coughs]

00:33:39.601 --> 00:33:41.186
[coughs]

00:33:45.107 --> 00:33:46.191
[church bells toll]

00:33:46.358 --> 00:33:47.651
[indistinct chatter]

00:33:53.073 --> 00:33:55.284
You saw these
things with your own eyes.

00:33:55.409 --> 00:33:56.535
Yes, Your Excellency.

00:33:56.744 --> 00:33:58.871
On land owned
rightly and duly by us--

00:33:58.996 --> 00:34:00.706
Well, the-- the Fairfaxes.

00:34:00.831 --> 00:34:03.625
I also own a significant
share of land there.

00:34:03.751 --> 00:34:05.586
This French encroachment
cannot stand.

00:34:05.711 --> 00:34:07.212
They must be told
to abandon it.

00:34:07.337 --> 00:34:09.882
By whom, sir? We don't
even know where they are.

00:34:10.007 --> 00:34:11.341
I do, sir.

00:34:11.800 --> 00:34:13.761
I could lead this expedition.

00:34:13.886 --> 00:34:16.096
To deliver your demands
to the French.

00:34:16.221 --> 00:34:18.098
I know the land, sir,
better than anyone.

00:34:18.223 --> 00:34:19.183
You?

00:34:19.349 --> 00:34:21.435
In the 15 years since the
Crown sent me to serve,

00:34:21.560 --> 00:34:24.480
I've yet to have a good
experience with a... colonist.

00:34:24.605 --> 00:34:26.148
Well, I look forward
to changing your opinion.

00:34:26.273 --> 00:34:27.941
If there used to be a
colonial expedition,

00:34:28.066 --> 00:34:29.860
it would be led
by your own brother.

00:34:29.985 --> 00:34:31.445
He commands the militia.

00:34:31.570 --> 00:34:33.030
Lawrences health fails him, sir.

00:34:33.155 --> 00:34:36.074
And he is no longer able to
fulfill the duties of his post.

00:34:36.366 --> 00:34:37.367
Here.

00:34:38.118 --> 00:34:40.704
He recommends me
as his replacement.

00:34:44.416 --> 00:34:46.043
So you have ambition?

00:34:46.168 --> 00:34:47.669
Yes, sir. I do.

00:34:48.295 --> 00:34:50.714
I see you met the savage
we call the Half-King.

00:34:50.839 --> 00:34:52.216
I have met the man.

00:34:52.341 --> 00:34:54.468
He led me to this information,
but...

00:34:54.593 --> 00:34:57.221
whether he can be trusted...
I’m not certain.

00:34:57.346 --> 00:34:59.640
I should be
alarmed if you were.

00:35:01.183 --> 00:35:03.352
Go and parley with
this Half-King,

00:35:03.477 --> 00:35:05.020
learn all you can from him.

00:35:05.145 --> 00:35:06.730
Then take your men
to Fort LeBoeuf,

00:35:06.855 --> 00:35:08.565
demand the French leave.

00:35:09.483 --> 00:35:12.569
My... my... my men, sir?

00:35:12.694 --> 00:35:16.198
Yes. Recruit 150
of your fellow Virginians.

00:35:16.532 --> 00:35:19.409
Lead them and
deliver this message.

00:35:20.327 --> 00:35:21.954
Which says what, sir?

00:35:22.079 --> 00:35:24.081
That they leave immediately.

00:35:24.665 --> 00:35:25.999
And if the French refuse?

00:35:26.124 --> 00:35:27.626
Do not permit them to refuse.

00:35:27.751 --> 00:35:29.044
So, then I am to fight?

00:35:29.169 --> 00:35:32.047
You are to deliver a message
and await further orders.

00:35:32.172 --> 00:35:33.340
[Gage] Your Excellency,
if I may.

00:35:33.465 --> 00:35:34.842
Will he not need the assistance

00:35:34.967 --> 00:35:36.802
of professional soldiers
of the Crown?

00:35:37.177 --> 00:35:41.390
No, militia will do. Especially
under one of such ambition.

00:35:42.432 --> 00:35:45.769
You shall receive the rank of
Major in the Virginia militia,

00:35:45.894 --> 00:35:47.980
which is not a
royal commission, understood?

00:35:48.105 --> 00:35:49.064
Mmm.

00:35:50.190 --> 00:35:54.486
There is an interpreter here.
Van Braam. Dutchman. Take him.

00:35:55.612 --> 00:35:58.198
Will my men and
I receive equal pay, sir?

00:35:58.448 --> 00:35:59.116
To whom?

00:36:00.242 --> 00:36:02.494
British officers of the Crown.

00:36:02.619 --> 00:36:04.830
Mr. Washington, you've just
advanced from farmer

00:36:04.955 --> 00:36:06.582
to Major in a
matter of seconds.

00:36:06.707 --> 00:36:09.334
What you ask for is
offensive to me.

00:36:09.459 --> 00:36:11.837
Then I will
volunteer my service.

00:36:12.254 --> 00:36:13.755
I have no need
to pay that is not equal

00:36:13.881 --> 00:36:16.967
to those of whom
I will prove myself equal.

00:36:17.426 --> 00:36:18.093
Sir.

00:36:19.887 --> 00:36:21.179
God save the King.

00:36:27.352 --> 00:36:28.520
[uplifting music]

00:36:31.607 --> 00:36:33.525
[Sally] I can't say
red becomes you, George.

00:36:34.026 --> 00:36:35.193
You don't think so?

00:36:35.319 --> 00:36:38.155
Well, even if I did,
I wouldn't say.

00:36:38.697 --> 00:36:40.073
[Sally] Thank you for
your letters.

00:36:40.908 --> 00:36:42.409
I read them all ten times over.

00:36:44.411 --> 00:36:47.998
At the river's fork, the world
widened as though God himself

00:36:48.123 --> 00:36:51.710
had drawn back the curtain
and whispered, "Begin."

00:36:53.921 --> 00:36:55.714
These are not surveyor’s notes.

00:36:55.839 --> 00:37:00.260
No. You love the frontier the
way poets love their first muse.

00:37:00.510 --> 00:37:01.511
Why?

00:37:02.137 --> 00:37:05.766
It loved me first, I guess.
Offered fairness.

00:37:06.266 --> 00:37:06.934
Fairness?

00:37:07.059 --> 00:37:10.646
Yes. Because the frontier is
new, wild, unclaimed.

00:37:11.188 --> 00:37:13.523
Vast enough to outrun
the old ways.

00:37:13.649 --> 00:37:17.736
And old rules? Like dowries and
fathers who barter daughters.

00:37:17.861 --> 00:37:22.157
Rules that say a man is measured
by ancestors you never met.

00:37:25.243 --> 00:37:28.330
Do you ever fear of
choosing incorrectly?

00:37:29.247 --> 00:37:32.960
That the path you seek might
vanish if you hesitate?

00:37:33.543 --> 00:37:36.838
The fear of not being able
to choose is worse.

00:37:39.007 --> 00:37:40.676
My fear is choosing.

00:37:41.468 --> 00:37:44.304
Then being told it was never
my choice to begin with.

00:37:44.429 --> 00:37:47.307
Then what would your choice be?

00:37:59.820 --> 00:38:03.865
If we were to follow
the river west, just you and I,

00:38:05.492 --> 00:38:07.577
what would we call that life?

00:38:09.162 --> 00:38:12.874
Wild. Beautiful.

00:38:13.583 --> 00:38:16.712
Dangerous. But, but free.

00:38:20.298 --> 00:38:23.301
I yearn for the
courage I see in you.

00:38:24.011 --> 00:38:26.930
And I, for the grace
you carry with ease.

00:38:30.475 --> 00:38:32.477
I should be getting back.

00:38:35.897 --> 00:38:36.690
Where?

00:38:37.315 --> 00:38:40.402
Another party.
Another performance.

00:38:43.780 --> 00:38:45.032
My solemn duty.

00:38:51.788 --> 00:38:54.041
[romantic music]

00:39:06.470 --> 00:39:07.888
[adventurous music]

00:39:24.988 --> 00:39:27.074
Congratulations on your first
command, Major.

00:39:27.199 --> 00:39:31.620
An army of outlaws,
debtors, slaves, and...

00:39:32.579 --> 00:39:33.330
[chuckles] well, patriots.

00:39:33.455 --> 00:39:35.207
Got any rum in
those carts?

00:39:35.332 --> 00:39:36.541
Only what’s rationed.

00:39:36.666 --> 00:39:38.168
Well, then ration us some.

00:39:38.418 --> 00:39:39.753
Back in line, Frisk.

00:39:39.878 --> 00:39:41.046
[Henry] Ain't no line.

00:39:41.421 --> 00:39:43.256
That snake trail is
the best we can do.

00:39:43.381 --> 00:39:45.217
It ain’t wide enough
for the carts.

00:39:45.342 --> 00:39:46.384
We should leave ‘em.

00:39:46.510 --> 00:39:48.595
Then how would we carry the rum?

00:39:48.720 --> 00:39:49.679
Fair point.

00:39:51.139 --> 00:39:52.015
Tucker!

00:39:52.599 --> 00:39:53.350
Yes, sir.

00:39:53.475 --> 00:39:55.310
We’ll camp here for the night.

00:39:55.435 --> 00:39:58.313
Ride ahead.
Make sure the road is clear.

00:40:05.195 --> 00:40:06.446
[Christopher] I wake
up at midnight,

00:40:06.571 --> 00:40:08.698
George is staring
into the woods.

00:40:08.824 --> 00:40:10.659
Propped against a tree,
musket in his lap.

00:40:11.034 --> 00:40:13.411
He says he's
been keepin' watch.

00:40:13.745 --> 00:40:15.205
You scared of the dark, George?

00:40:15.622 --> 00:40:17.499
George, you remember?

00:40:17.624 --> 00:40:18.959
[men laugh]

00:40:19.251 --> 00:40:20.377
Another love letter.

00:40:20.502 --> 00:40:21.920
[laughing]

00:40:22.629 --> 00:40:24.548
[Christopher] That woman's
gonna make you soft.

00:40:24.923 --> 00:40:26.591
[horse neighs]

00:40:31.555 --> 00:40:33.056
It's Tucker's horse.

00:40:44.276 --> 00:40:45.402
[muskets cracking]

00:40:46.820 --> 00:40:47.904
Van Braam.

00:40:50.115 --> 00:40:52.033
What business do you have with us?

00:40:53.034 --> 00:40:55.579
We have no conflict with you.

00:40:55.871 --> 00:40:57.872
We are only here...

00:40:57.873 --> 00:40:59.541
To speak to the French.

00:41:01.418 --> 00:41:02.794
We meet again.

00:41:05.213 --> 00:41:07.090
I'm Tanacharison.

00:41:07.215 --> 00:41:08.758
Of the Seneca nation.

00:41:08.884 --> 00:41:10.886
You ride on land we call home.

00:41:11.011 --> 00:41:14.514
The Governor assures
me you're willing to aid us.

00:41:15.348 --> 00:41:19.019
Many Indians are aligned
with the French. Why aren't you?

00:41:19.144 --> 00:41:20.562
I know their nature.

00:41:21.855 --> 00:41:23.356
And their intentions.

00:41:24.441 --> 00:41:25.525
What are yours?

00:41:25.817 --> 00:41:27.319
To demand they leave.

00:41:27.652 --> 00:41:29.154
And when they do not?

00:41:29.988 --> 00:41:30.947
That's not my decision.

00:41:31.072 --> 00:41:31.823
And yet you are here.

00:41:31.948 --> 00:41:34.576
Yes, and I would
greatly appreciate

00:41:34.701 --> 00:41:36.620
any help you
could give us.

00:41:42.500 --> 00:41:43.919
What are you called?

00:41:45.545 --> 00:41:46.213
George.

00:41:48.006 --> 00:41:49.799
Major George Washington.

00:42:02.395 --> 00:42:04.898
The French fort is
a day from here.

00:42:07.067 --> 00:42:08.318
We can take you.

00:42:08.985 --> 00:42:10.654
[ominous music]

00:42:40.517 --> 00:42:42.060
Why are you here?

00:43:01.079 --> 00:43:04.082
Why do you hate them?

00:43:06.293 --> 00:43:08.502
When I was a child

00:43:08.503 --> 00:43:09.045
I was taken captive by the French

00:43:09.045 --> 00:43:10.505
[horse neighing]

00:43:13.633 --> 00:43:18.345
I watched them boil my father.

00:43:18.346 --> 00:43:22.142
And eat him.

00:43:29.149 --> 00:43:32.652
From the royal Governor of Virginia:

00:43:32.694 --> 00:43:37.907
Sir, the lands upon the Ohio River
are notoriously known

00:43:37.949 --> 00:43:41.786
to be the property
of the Crown of Great Britain

00:43:41.828 --> 00:43:45.165
that it is a matter of equal concern
and surprise to hear that a body of

00:43:45.206 --> 00:43:51.045
French forces are erecting fortresses
within His Majesty's dominions.

00:43:51.046 --> 00:43:52.464
His dominion?

00:43:54.674 --> 00:43:56.217
Continue.

00:43:57.260 --> 00:44:01.556
In the name of the King, my master,
I have sent the bearer hereof,

00:44:01.598 --> 00:44:03.224
Major George Washington,

00:44:03.266 --> 00:44:08.063
one of the Adjutants-General
of this British Dominion.

00:44:10.857 --> 00:44:12.317
You are the Major?

00:44:12.734 --> 00:44:14.069
or his aide?

00:44:14.527 --> 00:44:16.112
I am Major Washington.

00:44:19.491 --> 00:44:20.617
[speaking French]

00:44:20.742 --> 00:44:22.786
[men laugh]

00:44:26.831 --> 00:44:28.917
[speaking French]

00:44:37.258 --> 00:44:40.053
He's inviting
us to dine with them.

00:44:46.893 --> 00:44:50.063
[ominous music]

00:44:58.446 --> 00:45:00.156
Can we speak in private?

00:45:02.075 --> 00:45:03.618
[speaking French]

00:45:07.330 --> 00:45:10.417
He says there's no
need to leave the table.

00:45:10.542 --> 00:45:11.501
We are all friends here.

00:45:12.168 --> 00:45:13.461
[Christopher speaking
Seneca]

00:45:16.297 --> 00:45:17.966
Know thy enemy indeed.

00:45:23.680 --> 00:45:27.267
So, how is it you are a Major?

00:45:29.769 --> 00:45:30.937
Do you even shave?

00:45:31.062 --> 00:45:32.564
[men laugh]

00:45:33.273 --> 00:45:35.358
You have no military service.

00:45:35.483 --> 00:45:36.609
Is it true?

00:45:37.610 --> 00:45:39.404
Magnifique.
You are not British,

00:45:39.529 --> 00:45:41.739
yet they send you
to speak for them.

00:45:42.532 --> 00:45:44.325
Why do you think that is?

00:45:45.577 --> 00:45:49.831
So that when you fail,
they'll have someone to blame.

00:45:52.250 --> 00:45:55.712
The King emphatically demands
you leave the Ohio country,

00:45:57.046 --> 00:45:59.257
and the territories altogether.

00:46:00.383 --> 00:46:03.761
This land has long been
claimed by the British Crown.

00:46:03.887 --> 00:46:05.722
And when was this?

00:46:05.847 --> 00:46:06.848
[in French] When?

00:46:07.724 --> 00:46:09.684
When did they claim it?

00:46:10.977 --> 00:46:12.479
You must withdraw.

00:46:12.604 --> 00:46:15.190
Because you
think you own this land?

00:46:17.192 --> 00:46:19.110
Who does own this land,

00:46:19.235 --> 00:46:21.446
if not the one who has
the will to tame it?

00:46:21.571 --> 00:46:23.114
[fists banging on the table]

00:46:24.657 --> 00:46:26.075
[indistinct chatter]

00:46:37.712 --> 00:46:39.547
I accept your message.

00:46:40.632 --> 00:46:42.383
You have delivered it.

00:46:43.343 --> 00:46:44.260
Now go.

00:46:46.387 --> 00:46:48.181
The King demands a reply.

00:46:54.229 --> 00:46:57.524
Then tell your King
we have claimed it.

00:46:59.359 --> 00:47:01.027
We will never leave.

00:47:01.819 --> 00:47:04.113
Then we will force you to leave.

00:47:05.156 --> 00:47:06.324
Oh.

00:47:09.369 --> 00:47:11.871
You do not want to start a war.

00:47:16.918 --> 00:47:19.295
Take your pet savage and go.

00:47:23.049 --> 00:47:24.551
[tense music]

00:47:28.638 --> 00:47:30.473
[George] Camp 15 miles
south of here.

00:47:30.640 --> 00:47:32.517
I’m going to ride ahead
and deliver the message.

00:47:32.642 --> 00:47:33.810
Should we send a scout?

00:47:33.935 --> 00:47:36.062
I'm the fastest scout we have.

00:47:36.187 --> 00:47:38.273
[ominous music]

00:48:02.547 --> 00:48:03.423
[door opens]

00:48:03.548 --> 00:48:04.507
Major.

00:48:05.883 --> 00:48:08.928
You will deliver
this ultimatum at once.

00:48:11.514 --> 00:48:13.766
The French spit in my face.

00:48:14.225 --> 00:48:15.435
Governor, with respect,
could you clarify--

00:48:15.560 --> 00:48:17.395
Transcribe all you have,
so I can report this

00:48:17.520 --> 00:48:19.647
to the council in the morning.

00:48:20.732 --> 00:48:21.649
Very well.

00:48:22.734 --> 00:48:24.485
Grant me one night’s rest
and fresh mounts.

00:48:24.611 --> 00:48:25.945
I’ve ridden
300 miles to--

00:48:26.070 --> 00:48:29.616
You will rest when
His Majesty's frontier rests.

00:48:29.741 --> 00:48:30.950
Before dawn, you'll present a

00:48:31.075 --> 00:48:32.744
full transcription
of your journal.

00:48:32.869 --> 00:48:35.580
Maps, strength estimates,
every scratch of observation,

00:48:35.705 --> 00:48:38.833
for the council's brief
at ten o'clock. Understood?

00:48:38.958 --> 00:48:39.709
Understood, sir.

00:48:39.834 --> 00:48:40.710
Good.

00:48:40.918 --> 00:48:42.962
Now go and prove
the Crown correct

00:48:43.087 --> 00:48:45.423
in placing
trust in a provincial.

00:48:50.011 --> 00:48:52.805
This is a dangerous escalation,
George.

00:48:53.848 --> 00:48:55.683
You are to deliver this?

00:48:57.101 --> 00:48:58.978
I've been ordered
to deliver this.

00:48:59.103 --> 00:49:00.480
You volunteered.

00:49:04.734 --> 00:49:05.401
No.

00:49:06.235 --> 00:49:08.071
- No, perhaps I can speak--
- No, no.

00:49:08.196 --> 00:49:09.822
This is the moment
I've been waiting for.

00:49:09.947 --> 00:49:11.949
I don't think it is, George.

00:49:14.369 --> 00:49:16.829
Why has no one else volunteered?

00:49:18.289 --> 00:49:21.793
Why does no British
officer lead this expedition?

00:49:26.422 --> 00:49:28.299
They’re using you, George.

00:49:28.758 --> 00:49:32.220
As a proxy.
To claim land for them.

00:49:33.221 --> 00:49:36.474
If you succeed,
they will rob you of the glory.

00:49:36.599 --> 00:49:38.976
If you fail, they'll have
a colonial to blame.

00:49:39.102 --> 00:49:39.977
Then I will not fail.

00:49:40.103 --> 00:49:41.688
If you do,
it could start a war.

00:49:41.813 --> 00:49:43.856
Thank you for your trust in me.

00:49:43.981 --> 00:49:45.692
That's not what I meant.

00:49:46.442 --> 00:49:49.862
I will claim it, and
I will earn their respect.

00:49:50.113 --> 00:49:52.824
That is what you
taught me, is it not?

00:49:52.949 --> 00:49:54.909
Besides, this is a new world.

00:49:55.076 --> 00:49:55.952
A new world?

00:49:56.452 --> 00:49:57.662
The soil may be new,

00:49:57.787 --> 00:49:59.872
but it’s owners still write
their ledgers in old ink.

00:49:59.997 --> 00:50:01.207
Let them write.

00:50:05.795 --> 00:50:10.633
You're betting your life on a
system designed to deny you.

00:50:11.551 --> 00:50:14.637
Every triumph you have
will be chalked up to luck,

00:50:14.762 --> 00:50:18.141
or the Native allies
or the British themselves.

00:50:18.349 --> 00:50:19.308
Never you.

00:50:19.434 --> 00:50:21.018
So I should stay here,

00:50:21.144 --> 00:50:24.897
mind the crops and live quietly
because I was born quietly?

00:50:25.022 --> 00:50:26.441
Do nothing with my life?

00:50:26.566 --> 00:50:28.151
Better alive and quiet

00:50:28.985 --> 00:50:30.737
than dead and forgotten
in the Alleghenies.

00:50:30.862 --> 00:50:31.988
You sound like mother.

00:50:32.113 --> 00:50:33.072
I speak the truth.

00:50:33.197 --> 00:50:34.782
[laughs] Well I would rather die
unknown than live

00:50:34.907 --> 00:50:37.034
believing the world’s
measure of me is fixed.

00:50:37.160 --> 00:50:39.162
That... that is pride.

00:50:39.287 --> 00:50:41.414
No, that is faith in what a man
can forge with his own hands.

00:50:41.539 --> 00:50:43.416
You cannot forge
your way into their system.

00:50:43.541 --> 00:50:44.250
And why not?

00:50:44.375 --> 00:50:45.960
Because that is not
the way the world works.

00:50:46.085 --> 00:50:47.336
Then someone should remake it.

00:50:47.462 --> 00:50:48.671
[Lawrence coughs]

00:50:52.133 --> 00:50:55.595
George, you
cannot change these things.

00:50:57.764 --> 00:51:00.266
You may well die trying.

00:51:03.561 --> 00:51:04.228
George--

00:51:04.353 --> 00:51:06.647
I wish you believed in me.

00:51:10.526 --> 00:51:12.653
[coughing]

00:51:18.743 --> 00:51:21.412
[soft string music]

00:51:21.537 --> 00:51:23.080
[indistinct chatter]

00:51:46.312 --> 00:51:47.396
[Sally] Major Washington.

00:51:47.522 --> 00:51:49.649
I thought you were leading
your men to the frontier.

00:51:49.774 --> 00:51:50.900
Tomorrow I am.

00:51:51.025 --> 00:51:52.777
But I have returned
on an urgent matter.

00:51:52.902 --> 00:51:54.237
I'll go back in the morning.

00:51:54.403 --> 00:51:56.697
But, tonight, I am here for you.

00:51:56.823 --> 00:51:58.199
[inaudible whispers]

00:51:59.367 --> 00:52:01.869
George, there is no
fairness here.

00:52:01.994 --> 00:52:04.497
Miss Cary—may I
have this dance?

00:52:04.872 --> 00:52:06.415
[string music plays]

00:52:06.833 --> 00:52:07.792
Yes, Major.

00:52:44.912 --> 00:52:48.416
George, I see
you found a tailor.

00:52:48.708 --> 00:52:49.625
Yes.

00:52:49.792 --> 00:52:51.961
Tonight I wear
His Majesty's commission.

00:52:52.086 --> 00:52:53.671
At dawn, I am
to lead 150 soldiers

00:52:53.796 --> 00:52:56.007
to demand the
French leave our land.

00:52:56.132 --> 00:52:59.468
Well, our land, to be precise.

00:52:59.927 --> 00:53:02.763
And this is not exactly
His Majesty's commission.

00:53:02.889 --> 00:53:05.516
Your uniform, however,
crimson, still prints colonial.

00:53:05.641 --> 00:53:06.350
William.

00:53:06.559 --> 00:53:09.562
It is a point I make
intentionally, Sally.

00:53:09.770 --> 00:53:12.315
I fear for you, George.

00:53:13.190 --> 00:53:16.569
And I question
our Governor's decision.

00:53:17.695 --> 00:53:21.032
If the situation
with the French is so dire,

00:53:21.157 --> 00:53:22.241
why would they not

00:53:22.366 --> 00:53:25.119
send professional
soldiers of the Crown?

00:53:25.244 --> 00:53:26.829
Because I volunteered.

00:53:27.830 --> 00:53:30.291
And if you care so much,
why didn't you?

00:53:30.416 --> 00:53:32.793
Because I have an estate to run.

00:53:33.794 --> 00:53:36.047
And I have a fortune to manage.

00:53:36.714 --> 00:53:38.674
And people depend on me.

00:53:40.384 --> 00:53:41.385
But...

00:53:42.511 --> 00:53:47.516
I can send along two of
my best slaves, Charles and Sam.

00:53:48.142 --> 00:53:52.229
Charles knows horses better than
most grooms in Virginia.

00:53:52.438 --> 00:53:56.150
Well, I wouldn't want
to deprive you of their labor.

00:53:56.317 --> 00:53:57.735
We have plenty.

00:53:58.069 --> 00:53:59.362
[Lord Fairfax] Major
Washington.

00:54:01.697 --> 00:54:05.117
Congratulations on
your rank and assignment.

00:54:05.368 --> 00:54:06.827
An astonishing rise.

00:54:07.912 --> 00:54:08.996
Thank you, sir.

00:54:09.372 --> 00:54:13.125
So, what think you of our young
William and Sally?

00:54:13.250 --> 00:54:13.918
Yes.

00:54:14.043 --> 00:54:16.629
Do they not make a,
a handsome couple?

00:54:17.254 --> 00:54:20.299
We are gathered
here to celebrate this.

00:54:20.716 --> 00:54:23.511
Their betrothal
is scarcely a week old.

00:54:25.137 --> 00:54:26.138
Uh...

00:54:26.263 --> 00:54:27.556
Indeed they do.

00:54:27.682 --> 00:54:28.808
Splendid!

00:54:28.933 --> 00:54:30.851
Now, may I propose a toast?

00:54:31.852 --> 00:54:35.272
To Major Washington—
who rides at first light...

00:54:35.398 --> 00:54:37.149
[speech fades behind music]

00:54:41.362 --> 00:54:42.947
[low rumbling sound]

00:54:43.114 --> 00:54:44.323
[Fairfax] Major Washington.

00:54:46.575 --> 00:54:48.035
William, Miss Cary.

00:54:48.577 --> 00:54:49.412
Forgive the stir.

00:54:49.537 --> 00:54:52.748
I look forward to returning
worthy of your investment...

00:54:52.873 --> 00:54:54.375
and your care.

00:54:56.127 --> 00:54:58.421
[soft music]

00:55:07.304 --> 00:55:08.806
[George] Act on the defensive

00:55:09.265 --> 00:55:12.101
But if any attempts are made to
disrupt our work or settlements,

00:55:12.226 --> 00:55:13.644
restrain all such offenders,

00:55:13.769 --> 00:55:17.440
and make prisoners of,
or kill and destroy, them.

00:55:18.774 --> 00:55:20.109
Well, that’s clear as mud.

00:55:20.234 --> 00:55:21.485
He cannot be serious.

00:55:21.610 --> 00:55:22.695
“Destroy them?”

00:55:22.820 --> 00:55:24.697
If it’s war he wants,
it's best to reinforce us

00:55:24.822 --> 00:55:26.032
with proper British soldiers.

00:55:26.157 --> 00:55:27.283
We ain't here to fight.

00:55:27.408 --> 00:55:28.200
Then why are you?

00:55:28.325 --> 00:55:29.201
To get paid.

00:55:29.410 --> 00:55:30.202
This is our duty.

00:55:30.327 --> 00:55:31.537
No, it ain't.

00:55:32.288 --> 00:55:34.832
We delivered his little letter.
We should leave.

00:55:34.957 --> 00:55:35.875
You will not.

00:55:36.625 --> 00:55:39.545
Or I will have
you flogged as a deserter.

00:55:40.671 --> 00:55:42.506
Now, we didn't
sign up for no war.

00:55:42.631 --> 00:55:44.133
You put on the coat!

00:55:45.009 --> 00:55:46.218
You took an oath.

00:55:47.553 --> 00:55:49.889
You have a duty, as do I.

00:55:53.392 --> 00:55:55.770
If this goes wrong,
he’ll blame Virginia.

00:55:55.895 --> 00:55:58.314
[George] Dinwiddie speaks
for the Crown.

00:55:59.815 --> 00:56:03.277
It's decided. This is a direct
order and we will obey it.

00:56:03.402 --> 00:56:04.612
It's not direct at all.

00:56:04.737 --> 00:56:06.697
Then your gods have
delivered you to war.

00:56:07.364 --> 00:56:08.365
It is not our intent.

00:56:08.491 --> 00:56:10.284
[Tucker] I found
their encampment.

00:56:11.535 --> 00:56:13.704
It’s much further south.
Much closer.

00:56:13.829 --> 00:56:14.538
How close?

00:56:14.914 --> 00:56:15.706
Five miles.

00:56:16.123 --> 00:56:18.709
[Tanacharison] He searches for
land to build another fort.

00:56:18.834 --> 00:56:22.254
To demand you abandon
the land he calls his own.

00:56:23.506 --> 00:56:24.590
Take me to him.

00:56:26.425 --> 00:56:28.844
A simple
reconnaissance. Agreed?

00:56:38.604 --> 00:56:41.107
[tense music]

00:57:08.175 --> 00:57:09.760
[Tanacharison] Drunk with
his own pride.

00:57:09.885 --> 00:57:13.472
He defies you and your King
by traveling this far.

00:57:18.561 --> 00:57:19.854
What will you do?

00:57:25.568 --> 00:57:26.986
Hold your ground.

00:57:28.112 --> 00:57:29.697
I'll tell them once
again to leave.

00:57:29.822 --> 00:57:31.991
What will you do
when they refuse?

00:57:32.116 --> 00:57:33.159
- Pray they--
- [gunshot]

00:57:38.622 --> 00:57:40.040
Who fired that shot?

00:57:41.667 --> 00:57:42.835
[gunshot]

00:57:45.796 --> 00:57:47.214
Hold your ground!

00:57:47.339 --> 00:57:48.174
Hold your ground!

00:57:48.299 --> 00:57:49.383
[yelling in French]

00:57:53.679 --> 00:57:55.055
[indian whoops and yells]

00:57:57.641 --> 00:57:59.018
[gunshots]

00:58:00.227 --> 00:58:01.937
[yelling in French]

00:58:15.534 --> 00:58:16.744
Forward!

00:58:23.459 --> 00:58:25.628
[yelling]

00:58:25.753 --> 00:58:28.422
[gunshots]

00:58:35.554 --> 00:58:36.639
Hold your fire!

00:58:37.139 --> 00:58:38.224
Hold your fire!

00:58:38.349 --> 00:58:39.433
Prisoners only!

00:58:39.558 --> 00:58:40.851
Prisoners only!

00:58:40.976 --> 00:58:41.644
Prisoners--

00:58:41.769 --> 00:58:43.979
[yelling]
[gunshot]

00:58:44.104 --> 00:58:45.564
[sigh]

00:58:45.689 --> 00:58:46.774
[sound of heartbeat]

00:58:50.236 --> 00:58:52.071
[sound of heartbeat]

00:58:52.196 --> 00:58:53.822
[soldier yells]

00:58:56.116 --> 00:58:58.619
[yelling]
[gunshots]

00:59:04.041 --> 00:59:06.252
We should have killed everyone of you.

00:59:12.258 --> 00:59:14.343
Thou art not yet dead, my father.

00:59:18.973 --> 00:59:20.224
- Wait!
- [Jumonville groans]

00:59:20.683 --> 00:59:21.767
Wait!

00:59:23.435 --> 00:59:25.312
[indian whoops and cheers]

00:59:29.942 --> 00:59:32.820
[George] I do not know who
fired that first shot,

00:59:33.237 --> 00:59:35.406
but in light of
these unfortunate events,

00:59:35.531 --> 00:59:39.118
I fear a war with the
French is indeed imminent.

00:59:39.994 --> 00:59:44.123
We are building a fort and
taking up a defensive position.

00:59:44.248 --> 00:59:46.166
In the spirit
of mutual benefit,

00:59:46.292 --> 00:59:49.670
please send reinforcements
to aid our endeavor.

00:59:52.381 --> 00:59:53.799
[David] Hey,
why don't we arm them?

00:59:54.091 --> 00:59:56.302
We need all the men we can get.

00:59:57.636 --> 00:59:59.179
They might shoot us.

01:00:00.097 --> 01:00:01.181
Wouldn't you?

01:00:01.890 --> 01:00:02.850
Fair point.

01:00:03.309 --> 01:00:04.476
- Gist!
- Yep.

01:00:07.229 --> 01:00:09.148
Permission to speak my mind.

01:00:09.273 --> 01:00:10.316
Never stopped you?

01:00:10.441 --> 01:00:11.442
[sarcastic laugh]

01:00:12.109 --> 01:00:14.028
Building this fort too low.

01:00:14.361 --> 01:00:15.779
What do you mean?

01:00:16.322 --> 01:00:17.406
The walls?

01:00:18.949 --> 01:00:20.492
No, not the walls--

01:00:20.617 --> 01:00:23.245
This here, this is a
dry lake bed.

01:00:23.996 --> 01:00:26.874
One good rain, it’ll flood out.

01:00:27.249 --> 01:00:31.170
Besides, I could shoot
every one of us from them trees.

01:00:35.174 --> 01:00:37.134
Major know what he’s doin?

01:00:41.055 --> 01:00:42.264
What you writing?

01:00:42.556 --> 01:00:44.558
Another plea for reinforcements.

01:00:45.100 --> 01:00:45.976
From who?

01:00:46.685 --> 01:00:47.644
Colonies.

01:00:49.021 --> 01:00:52.232
Pennsylvania don't care
about Virginia's problems.

01:00:52.358 --> 01:00:55.361
The French are the
concern of all. Agreed?

01:00:57.237 --> 01:00:59.198
This area lies awfully low.

01:01:00.074 --> 01:01:01.950
The forest gives us cover.

01:01:02.534 --> 01:01:03.827
The great meadows offer
plenty of space

01:01:03.952 --> 01:01:05.871
and a clear view
of any oncoming threats.

01:01:05.996 --> 01:01:07.831
If they attack,
it'll be from the front.

01:01:07.956 --> 01:01:11.627
Or, we'll be easy
targets, when the fort floods.

01:01:14.963 --> 01:01:16.799
Well, Gist, what would
you have me do?

01:01:16.924 --> 01:01:18.133
Major Washington.

01:01:18.842 --> 01:01:19.802
The King's troops.

01:01:19.927 --> 01:01:21.053
What about them?

01:01:21.553 --> 01:01:22.971
[Tucker] They're here.

01:01:45.619 --> 01:01:46.995
Where's Washington?

01:01:47.287 --> 01:01:48.455
I am Major Washington.

01:01:48.622 --> 01:01:49.331
[scoffs]

01:01:49.706 --> 01:01:51.208
Captain James Mackay.

01:01:52.376 --> 01:01:54.586
Orders from Governor Dinwiddie.

01:01:56.046 --> 01:01:58.924
We are here to reinforce
the Virginia Regiment

01:01:59.049 --> 01:02:02.636
and deal with this...
situation you’ve created.

01:02:03.887 --> 01:02:06.557
French and Indian soldiers.
Professional soldiers.

01:02:06.682 --> 01:02:08.267
Are nearly upon us.

01:02:08.392 --> 01:02:10.310
Over a thousand in total.

01:02:10.436 --> 01:02:13.605
They are commanded by
Louis Coulon de Villiers.

01:02:13.730 --> 01:02:17.192
Brother to Joseph Coulon
de Villiers de Jumonville.

01:02:17.317 --> 01:02:19.486
The man who you killed.

01:02:24.408 --> 01:02:26.493
This letter says Colonel
Joshua Fry is in command.

01:02:26.618 --> 01:02:28.120
Oh, the boy can read.

01:02:28.495 --> 01:02:29.371
Where is he?

01:02:29.496 --> 01:02:30.497
Dead.

01:02:31.081 --> 01:02:34.209
Fell from his horse two
days ago and broke his neck.

01:02:34.334 --> 01:02:38.213
You are to assume his rank
as Colonel, Mr. Washington.

01:02:40.132 --> 01:02:41.508
[George] Well then, welcome.

01:02:41.842 --> 01:02:44.094
We need all
the help we can get.

01:02:44.219 --> 01:02:45.929
I do not take orders from you.

01:02:46.054 --> 01:02:47.055
But...

01:02:47.598 --> 01:02:49.475
you said I was to
assume the rank is Colonel.

01:02:49.600 --> 01:02:51.226
My commission is royal.

01:02:51.477 --> 01:02:54.480
You could be a general and I
wouldn't have to listen to you.

01:02:54.605 --> 01:02:55.397
Praise God.

01:02:56.482 --> 01:02:59.902
Now, what do
you call this... fort?

01:03:00.736 --> 01:03:02.779
Well, it was made by necessity.

01:03:02.905 --> 01:03:04.281
So I think
that's a fitting name.

01:03:04.406 --> 01:03:05.407
Mmm.

01:03:06.074 --> 01:03:08.368
We will camp 100 yards
to the front.

01:03:08.494 --> 01:03:11.580
No doubt the French
will engage us there.

01:03:11.747 --> 01:03:13.332
Colonel.

01:03:13.540 --> 01:03:14.541
Van Braam.

01:03:19.630 --> 01:03:20.547
[Mackay] The boy can read.

01:03:20.672 --> 01:03:21.757
[Mackay chuckles]

01:03:26.053 --> 01:03:28.055
[water splashing]

01:03:29.431 --> 01:03:31.183
[thunder booms]

01:03:47.991 --> 01:03:49.368
How's the progress?

01:03:49.576 --> 01:03:52.329
Ditch is taking in water
faster than we can throw it.

01:03:52.454 --> 01:03:55.165
I say, this keeps up.

01:03:55.374 --> 01:03:59.169
I’ll commission my men to
construct a Royal Navy.

01:03:59.294 --> 01:04:00.379
Keep trying.

01:04:03.257 --> 01:04:05.008
I could shoot you
from the trees.

01:04:05.133 --> 01:04:06.969
The French won’t fire
from the trees.

01:04:07.094 --> 01:04:11.098
They’ll assemble in open fields.
To fight with honor.

01:04:11.306 --> 01:04:13.433
You call this
land the New World?

01:04:13.559 --> 01:04:15.394
Yet you live by the old ways.

01:04:15.519 --> 01:04:17.521
They will lead you to death.

01:04:17.729 --> 01:04:19.856
Any recruits among the Shawnee?

01:04:19.982 --> 01:04:20.649
No.

01:04:20.774 --> 01:04:22.693
What about the Delaware
or the Mingo?

01:04:22.818 --> 01:04:25.195
No. Some have
even joined the French.

01:04:25.320 --> 01:04:26.780
None will aid you.

01:04:28.782 --> 01:04:30.158
Neither will we.

01:04:31.159 --> 01:04:32.536
You will not leave!

01:04:34.496 --> 01:04:36.164
Your vengeance started this.

01:04:36.290 --> 01:04:38.166
And your stubbornness
will be the end of it.

01:04:38.292 --> 01:04:39.918
The French are cowards.

01:04:40.043 --> 01:04:41.628
The British are fools.

01:04:41.753 --> 01:04:43.755
You do not
know how to fight here.

01:04:43.880 --> 01:04:46.300
I was born here on
this land, as were you.

01:04:46.425 --> 01:04:48.802
Can we not
fight for it together?

01:04:49.511 --> 01:04:53.390
This land
does not belong to you.

01:04:53.515 --> 01:04:55.392
While you kill each other,

01:04:56.101 --> 01:04:57.686
we wait to reclaim it.

01:05:00.105 --> 01:05:03.233
[Christopher] George, you made
the wrong choice of ground.

01:05:03.567 --> 01:05:07.654
Admit it. That's it, It's
alright, it's alright. Admit it.

01:05:07.779 --> 01:05:09.114
Our supplies are exhausted.

01:05:09.239 --> 01:05:11.241
We’ve two days' rations at best.

01:05:11.366 --> 01:05:15.329
Move camp and save the men.

01:05:18.498 --> 01:05:20.208
We will stand our ground.

01:05:27.466 --> 01:05:29.092
Any sign of the French?

01:05:29.509 --> 01:05:31.595
Nothing. No doubt the arrival
of actual soldiers

01:05:31.720 --> 01:05:33.263
put a stop
to their advancements.

01:05:33.388 --> 01:05:37.100
But listen, my men are
camping in what is now a swamp.

01:05:37.225 --> 01:05:38.769
What do you want me to do?

01:05:38.894 --> 01:05:40.062
Find solid ground.

01:05:40.187 --> 01:05:42.731
Or better yet, an
experienced commander.

01:05:42.856 --> 01:05:44.858
Are you
challenging my authority?

01:05:44.983 --> 01:05:46.485
[scoffs] You have no authority.

01:05:46.652 --> 01:05:47.819
- [gunshot]
- [Mackay grunts]

01:05:54.409 --> 01:05:57.412
Trees! They're in the trees!
Take cover!

01:05:57.537 --> 01:05:58.789
- [horse neighs]
- [gunshots boom]

01:06:02.834 --> 01:06:04.169
[yelling and gunshots]

01:06:05.295 --> 01:06:06.463
Move, move.

01:06:06.672 --> 01:06:07.547
Go, go, go.

01:06:07.673 --> 01:06:08.465
Grab a musket.

01:06:09.299 --> 01:06:10.926
Move, move, move, move!

01:06:11.843 --> 01:06:12.803
[George] Hold the line.

01:06:13.220 --> 01:06:14.513
Form a line on me.

01:06:14.638 --> 01:06:16.598
A line? Yeah, a smart idea.

01:06:20.727 --> 01:06:21.728
Fire!

01:06:26.108 --> 01:06:27.651
They’re firing from all sides.

01:06:27.776 --> 01:06:29.277
To the front with me!

01:06:31.363 --> 01:06:33.573
Form up! On me, on me.

01:06:36.451 --> 01:06:37.119
Christopher.

01:06:37.244 --> 01:06:37.911
Yeah?

01:06:38.328 --> 01:06:40.580
Divide the men. Keep 50 in
the fort and fire to the trees.

01:06:40.706 --> 01:06:42.541
50 won’t fit in the fort,
it’s flooded out.

01:06:42.666 --> 01:06:43.750
As many as you can, then.

01:06:43.875 --> 01:06:45.836
All right men on me!
Move, move, move, move.

01:06:45.961 --> 01:06:47.295
Everyone to the front line.

01:06:47.421 --> 01:06:48.088
Present.

01:06:49.047 --> 01:06:50.048
Fire!

01:06:52.551 --> 01:06:54.386
[Henry] George, cannons!

01:06:59.433 --> 01:07:00.809
[David] George,
what's the plan, here?

01:07:01.435 --> 01:07:02.477
Second rank!

01:07:02.602 --> 01:07:03.812
Forward!

01:07:05.480 --> 01:07:06.481
Present!

01:07:08.859 --> 01:07:09.735
Make ready!

01:07:10.235 --> 01:07:11.403
Fire!

01:07:13.780 --> 01:07:15.198
[bullets whizzing]

01:07:17.701 --> 01:07:18.994
Fire!

01:07:24.124 --> 01:07:25.584
[men yell]

01:07:28.545 --> 01:07:29.421
Retreat!

01:07:30.547 --> 01:07:31.798
Back to the fort.

01:07:42.851 --> 01:07:44.936
Back to the fort. Get inside!

01:07:52.527 --> 01:07:53.445
[George] Move!

01:07:53.570 --> 01:07:56.156
Get inside! Get inside!

01:07:56.990 --> 01:07:57.657
[George] Move!

01:07:59.743 --> 01:08:01.828
[men yelling]

01:08:05.081 --> 01:08:06.625
Come on. Get in!

01:08:07.626 --> 01:08:08.543
Get in there!

01:08:09.544 --> 01:08:10.337
[George] Get inside!

01:08:11.505 --> 01:08:12.172
Inside!

01:08:12.339 --> 01:08:13.507
[Christopher] George!
George!

01:08:13.632 --> 01:08:15.008
[George] Barricade the door!

01:08:15.175 --> 01:08:16.092
[George] Hold!

01:08:16.676 --> 01:08:18.220
- [cannon fire booms]
- [men yelling]

01:08:20.305 --> 01:08:21.681
[Henry] Powder’s wet.

01:08:21.807 --> 01:08:22.891
Nothing's firin'!

01:08:23.016 --> 01:08:24.601
We’re sittin’ ducks here,
Colonel.

01:08:24.726 --> 01:08:26.144
We keep fighting!

01:08:26.269 --> 01:08:27.395
Attach bayonets!

01:08:27.646 --> 01:08:29.022
The battle is lost.

01:08:29.231 --> 01:08:30.398
The battle is just begun.

01:08:30.524 --> 01:08:31.191
George!

01:08:31.650 --> 01:08:32.692
Man your post!

01:08:32.818 --> 01:08:33.610
Man your posts!

01:08:33.735 --> 01:08:34.486
Washington!

01:08:34.611 --> 01:08:35.445
Save your men!

01:08:35.570 --> 01:08:38.281
I will not
surrender my first command.

01:08:38.657 --> 01:08:39.491
Advance troops!

01:08:40.033 --> 01:08:41.326
They're coming in.

01:08:42.494 --> 01:08:43.620
Man your posts!

01:08:48.500 --> 01:08:49.960
Hold, hold, hold!

01:08:50.085 --> 01:08:51.169
[Christopher grunts]

01:08:59.302 --> 01:09:00.220
Gist!

01:09:00.554 --> 01:09:02.055
Gist!

01:09:05.267 --> 01:09:06.893
Just breathe, just breathe.

01:09:07.602 --> 01:09:08.687
Hey, hey.

01:09:09.437 --> 01:09:11.147
You're gonna be okay.
You're gonna be okay.

01:09:11.273 --> 01:09:15.235
Breathe, breathe,
breathe, I'm sorry.

01:09:16.152 --> 01:09:18.780
[sound muffles
behind music]

01:09:40.886 --> 01:09:41.928
Major!

01:09:45.765 --> 01:09:46.766
Yes.

01:09:48.518 --> 01:09:49.686
[George] Surrender.

01:09:50.562 --> 01:09:52.439
[solemn music]

01:09:55.525 --> 01:09:57.152
I'm sorry, Christopher.

01:09:57.360 --> 01:09:58.695
I am so sorry!

01:10:45.408 --> 01:10:46.534
[Jacob] Washington.

01:10:52.999 --> 01:10:55.251
Terms are somewhat favorable.

01:10:55.752 --> 01:10:57.796
It's a mutual withdrawal.

01:10:58.254 --> 01:10:59.965
They take our artillery,

01:11:00.215 --> 01:11:01.800
we'll remove the flag.

01:11:02.467 --> 01:11:05.387
And also they demand
you take responsibility

01:11:05.512 --> 01:11:08.390
for their commander's
unfortunate death.

01:11:10.892 --> 01:11:12.602
We didn't start this.

01:11:14.646 --> 01:11:17.440
Nobody knows
who fired that first shot.

01:11:20.276 --> 01:11:22.612
I've offered myself as security.

01:11:22.737 --> 01:11:24.197
I will go with them.

01:11:26.324 --> 01:11:29.411
This is the best
possible outcome, Colonel.

01:11:40.088 --> 01:11:41.297
Colonel.

01:11:52.350 --> 01:11:53.977
What is the date today?

01:11:54.602 --> 01:11:55.770
July third.

01:11:56.187 --> 01:11:58.565
July the third will be
etched in my memory forever.

01:12:10.368 --> 01:12:12.245
[solemn music]

01:13:18.019 --> 01:13:19.229
I'm so sorry.

01:13:20.897 --> 01:13:22.398
I'm so, so sorry.

01:13:33.076 --> 01:13:34.577
[Dinwiddie]
Assassination.

01:13:35.036 --> 01:13:38.456
You confessed to assassinating
a French Officer!

01:13:38.957 --> 01:13:40.583
It was not my intention,
Your Excellency.

01:13:40.708 --> 01:13:42.627
Is this not your signature?

01:13:44.796 --> 01:13:46.881
Our intention had
never been to trouble peace,

01:13:47.006 --> 01:13:48.383
but only to revenge

01:13:48.508 --> 01:13:51.511
the assassination of
one of our officers.

01:13:51.636 --> 01:13:52.720
The translator failed me, sir.

01:13:52.846 --> 01:13:54.264
I didn't realize.
I thought that--

01:13:54.389 --> 01:13:55.515
Washington.

01:13:55.723 --> 01:13:58.977
To lead is to forfeit
the right to make excuses.

01:13:59.769 --> 01:14:02.105
Have you any
idea what you've done?

01:14:02.272 --> 01:14:04.232
You've started a war!
[slams desk]

01:14:06.359 --> 01:14:07.777
I'll report that
the battle was lost

01:14:07.902 --> 01:14:10.029
due to poor munitions
and lack of supplies.

01:14:10.155 --> 01:14:12.365
But that is not the truth, sir.

01:14:12.574 --> 01:14:15.076
That is the truth
that suits me, otherwise--

01:14:15.201 --> 01:14:18.163
Sir, I came here
to resign my commission.

01:14:21.499 --> 01:14:23.251
I am not fit to lead.

01:14:24.335 --> 01:14:26.337
I was never fit to lead.

01:14:30.758 --> 01:14:32.051
God save the King.

01:14:35.763 --> 01:14:39.309
And your resignation would
say that I'm not fit to choose.

01:14:39.434 --> 01:14:41.644
Washington, you
abandon this office,

01:14:41.769 --> 01:14:44.606
you abandon your
ambition with it.

01:14:45.106 --> 01:14:46.232
Understood, sir.

01:15:20.350 --> 01:15:21.768
Where's Lawrence?

01:15:27.315 --> 01:15:28.816
I'm sorry.

01:15:50.588 --> 01:15:51.881
[screams]

01:16:07.397 --> 01:16:09.899
He wanted you
to have his journals.

01:16:13.194 --> 01:16:14.570
You were right.

01:16:16.114 --> 01:16:17.907
You knew I would fail.

01:16:19.075 --> 01:16:20.910
It's not your fault, George.

01:16:21.035 --> 01:16:24.455
You did not lay your
brother low. Nor those men.

01:16:26.708 --> 01:16:28.084
I chose the ground.

01:16:28.626 --> 01:16:30.628
I put on the coat.
I gave the order.

01:16:30.753 --> 01:16:32.630
And now
because of that...

01:16:35.258 --> 01:16:36.759
Good men are dead.

01:16:45.727 --> 01:16:47.562
When your father died,

01:16:48.521 --> 01:16:52.567
there were accounts
I could not read,

01:16:53.443 --> 01:16:58.281
acres I could not plow.
But I learned, as women do,

01:16:59.198 --> 01:17:03.995
to keep a tally with one hand
and a prayer with the other.

01:17:04.120 --> 01:17:09.459
I hardened because
the wind here is hard.

01:17:10.168 --> 01:17:12.587
Put iron in my voice.

01:17:14.047 --> 01:17:15.965
I was hard on you, George.

01:17:17.258 --> 01:17:21.679
I see you learned
to be hard on yourself.

01:17:22.555 --> 01:17:23.890
That was my sin.

01:17:34.025 --> 01:17:36.527
You said Providence
placed me here.

01:17:41.282 --> 01:17:42.200
Why?

01:17:43.993 --> 01:17:45.536
For me to fail?

01:17:46.496 --> 01:17:47.330
Perhaps.

01:17:49.749 --> 01:17:52.126
Failure is
the tutor sent by God.

01:17:53.169 --> 01:17:55.463
If you don't learn from it,
you've failed twice.

01:17:55.588 --> 01:17:59.050
If you do learn from it,
you've earned wisdom.

01:18:00.760 --> 01:18:01.552
So...

01:18:03.137 --> 01:18:04.639
What did it tell you?

01:18:06.974 --> 01:18:08.017
To go back.

01:18:12.188 --> 01:18:13.606
But I'm afraid...

01:18:14.690 --> 01:18:16.150
of making the same mistakes.

01:18:20.780 --> 01:18:25.701
War is not the path I would
choose for you. But...

01:18:26.661 --> 01:18:27.537
Oh...

01:18:27.995 --> 01:18:29.997
On your feet, son.

01:18:33.543 --> 01:18:39.090
If you must
return to soldiering, go.

01:18:41.968 --> 01:18:46.097
As God's servant.
Do it with your whole heart.

01:18:47.723 --> 01:18:48.975
Find your path.

01:18:49.934 --> 01:18:50.935
Make it yours.

01:18:51.519 --> 01:18:52.728
Make it straight.

01:18:55.523 --> 01:18:57.108
And prove them wrong.

01:19:02.238 --> 01:19:05.533
Because even a
pawn can take the king.

01:19:18.629 --> 01:19:21.340
[dramatic music]

01:19:43.821 --> 01:19:45.615
[drum beat plays]

01:20:08.054 --> 01:20:09.639
I'm sorry to disturb, sir.

01:20:10.389 --> 01:20:11.807
I am George Washington.

01:20:11.933 --> 01:20:12.600
Ah!

01:20:14.018 --> 01:20:15.728
The reason I am here.

01:20:16.979 --> 01:20:18.814
Meet Colonel Thomas Gage.

01:20:20.066 --> 01:20:22.151
Gage has recently
been promoted to colonel

01:20:22.276 --> 01:20:23.694
by Royal Commission.

01:20:24.153 --> 01:20:25.112
We’ve met.

01:20:25.404 --> 01:20:28.533
I'm assuming you
seek your previous command.

01:20:28.658 --> 01:20:30.993
Gage has been tasked
with leading your militia

01:20:31.118 --> 01:20:33.287
and is far more qualified.

01:20:33.788 --> 01:20:34.997
I'm sure he is.

01:20:35.289 --> 01:20:37.333
I neither ask for rank nor pay.

01:20:37.458 --> 01:20:39.460
I'm here to volunteer
as your aide-de-camp.

01:20:39.585 --> 01:20:41.045
I believe I could be
of some assistance to you.

01:20:41.170 --> 01:20:42.547
Oh, do not worry.

01:20:42.797 --> 01:20:45.967
Young Washington. These uh,
these French and their savages

01:20:46.092 --> 01:20:49.554
may have been a formidable enemy
to you and your militia,

01:20:49.679 --> 01:20:53.808
but to the King's troops, they
are more of a nuisance, really.

01:20:53.933 --> 01:20:56.018
Bit of a waste of powder.

01:20:56.352 --> 01:20:58.688
We will prevail. With ease.

01:20:58.813 --> 01:20:59.897
But with all due respect, sir,

01:21:00.022 --> 01:21:02.149
I do not think
it will be with ease.

01:21:02.275 --> 01:21:04.193
- Having fought--
- And lost.

01:21:04.402 --> 01:21:06.195
Having fought
within the region, sir,

01:21:06.320 --> 01:21:08.030
I believe I could
be of some help to you.

01:21:08.155 --> 01:21:09.615
Fort Duquesne is difficult.

01:21:09.740 --> 01:21:13.703
Duquesne can hardly detain me
above three or four days.

01:21:13.828 --> 01:21:16.289
Sir, this is a very
different type of battle.

01:21:16.414 --> 01:21:18.332
Just the trip to the fort
alone is treach--

01:21:18.457 --> 01:21:19.500
A week at most.

01:21:19.625 --> 01:21:20.334
A month.

01:21:21.252 --> 01:21:22.044
A month?

01:21:22.295 --> 01:21:23.212
If lucky.

01:21:24.505 --> 01:21:25.214
For most of the journey,

01:21:25.339 --> 01:21:26.465
you'll be
traveling a single file.

01:21:26.591 --> 01:21:28.384
over what is barely a trail.

01:21:28.509 --> 01:21:30.428
Not even wide enough for wagons.

01:21:30.553 --> 01:21:31.512
I've surveyed the land.

01:21:31.637 --> 01:21:32.847
I know this land.

01:21:33.347 --> 01:21:35.683
The French are located here,
where the three rivers meet.

01:21:35.808 --> 01:21:38.102
Because of the land, the style
of warfare is, uh,

01:21:38.227 --> 01:21:39.687
it's different.

01:21:40.062 --> 01:21:41.314
These are not the
open battlefields

01:21:41.439 --> 01:21:42.315
to which you're accustomed.

01:21:42.440 --> 01:21:45.401
I have fought on
a great many battlefields.

01:21:45.526 --> 01:21:46.861
Not in the new world, sir.

01:21:46.986 --> 01:21:48.988
You lost in the new world.

01:21:52.950 --> 01:21:54.243
Yes.

01:21:54.410 --> 01:21:55.536
You're right.

01:21:55.828 --> 01:21:58.039
But failure is a great teacher.

01:22:00.458 --> 01:22:01.834
I desire to serve under
someone of your ability

01:22:01.959 --> 01:22:04.045
and experience to learn more.

01:22:04.545 --> 01:22:05.338
Sir.

01:22:11.010 --> 01:22:14.388
You may come. As advisor
and aide. That is all.

01:22:15.514 --> 01:22:16.891
Thank you, General Braddock.

01:22:17.016 --> 01:22:19.644
Colonel Gage see
that he is accommodated.

01:22:19.769 --> 01:22:20.853
Yes, sir.

01:22:24.607 --> 01:22:26.901
[drum beat plays]

01:22:56.806 --> 01:22:58.099
[Braddock] What is the delay?

01:22:58.307 --> 01:22:59.350
Move these wagons.

01:22:59.475 --> 01:23:00.810
So, Washington.

01:23:02.144 --> 01:23:06.232
From colonel to aide-de-camp,
How the mighty have fallen.

01:23:06.440 --> 01:23:09.443
Well, I was never given
the Royal Commission as colonel,

01:23:09.568 --> 01:23:11.195
so did it truly matter?

01:23:12.780 --> 01:23:14.281
This is important to you?

01:23:14.407 --> 01:23:15.574
Fairness? Yes.

01:23:16.617 --> 01:23:19.912
Gage, what on
God's earth is the delay here?

01:23:20.287 --> 01:23:21.455
Fallen tree, I believe, sir.

01:23:21.580 --> 01:23:22.873
Well, how-how do you expect
to win a battle

01:23:22.998 --> 01:23:24.500
if you can't
even defeat a tree?

01:23:24.625 --> 01:23:25.292
Yes, sir.

01:23:25.793 --> 01:23:29.714
I have fought the King's battles
on three continents,

01:23:29.964 --> 01:23:32.883
but never have I
been defeated by a tree.

01:23:33.801 --> 01:23:35.594
[Braddock] This is no army.

01:23:35.803 --> 01:23:38.180
This is a centipede with gout.

01:23:40.391 --> 01:23:43.144
[Tucker] Henry, David.
Look who's here.

01:23:46.063 --> 01:23:47.022
Major?

01:23:47.273 --> 01:23:48.899
Aide-de-camp.

01:23:49.692 --> 01:23:52.236
It seems you're my
superiors, actually.

01:23:53.320 --> 01:23:55.781
Take up an axe
and help us with this tree.

01:23:56.282 --> 01:23:57.158
Gladly.

01:24:04.457 --> 01:24:06.292
[Gage] What seems to
be the delay?

01:24:06.417 --> 01:24:07.918
I'm sorry, Colonel.

01:24:08.419 --> 01:24:09.920
There's no damn road.

01:24:10.963 --> 01:24:12.173
That's the delay.

01:24:13.632 --> 01:24:15.760
[Gage] Washington,
these are your friends?

01:24:16.302 --> 01:24:18.137
Why do they not wear
the King’s red?

01:24:18.262 --> 01:24:19.096
Or at least try?

01:24:19.221 --> 01:24:21.348
You stole our last uniforms.

01:24:21.891 --> 01:24:23.726
Thievin' bastards.

01:24:24.226 --> 01:24:27.313
See, uh, indigo
grows wild around here.

01:24:27.813 --> 01:24:29.148
We use it for blue dye.

01:24:29.273 --> 01:24:30.483
That's the color of Virginia.

01:24:30.608 --> 01:24:31.817
You boys go’head,

01:24:31.942 --> 01:24:34.987
wear all them pretty colors
and get shot first.

01:24:35.112 --> 01:24:38.324
I’ll blend into the woods
and die an ol’ man.

01:24:44.455 --> 01:24:47.082
What happened
with your grand design?

01:24:48.125 --> 01:24:49.585
Royal commission.

01:24:50.753 --> 01:24:51.962
Little rich girl.

01:24:52.505 --> 01:24:55.883
I buried those plans
when I buried Christopher.

01:25:03.265 --> 01:25:04.683
Why'd you come back?

01:25:05.309 --> 01:25:07.311
Came back to apologize.

01:25:08.521 --> 01:25:10.231
My ambition was selfish.

01:25:10.731 --> 01:25:13.400
I owe a debt to
every single one of you.

01:25:13.526 --> 01:25:15.611
A debt I cannot repay, but...

01:25:16.946 --> 01:25:21.492
When the time comes
for battle, I will be there.

01:25:21.951 --> 01:25:23.911
Fighting beside you.

01:25:26.997 --> 01:25:28.082
Works for me.

01:25:30.543 --> 01:25:31.710
[Henry chuckles]

01:25:41.387 --> 01:25:42.721
[low rumbling sound]

01:25:42.847 --> 01:25:44.098
[metal clinking]

01:25:47.142 --> 01:25:49.645
[David] You need to place
a wager, George.

01:25:53.274 --> 01:25:56.861
How about you, uh,
how about you place one for me?

01:26:00.072 --> 01:26:02.074
You sure you're all right?

01:26:03.450 --> 01:26:05.327
Yeah, never better.

01:26:08.789 --> 01:26:11.041
- Thank you.
- Of course.

01:26:15.379 --> 01:26:17.006
Excuse me.

01:26:19.842 --> 01:26:21.385
Why are y'all here?

01:26:22.052 --> 01:26:23.137
We were sent.

01:26:23.345 --> 01:26:24.013
By who?

01:26:24.346 --> 01:26:25.639
The Fairfaxes.

01:26:25.806 --> 01:26:27.266
You'll fight for nobles?

01:26:27.391 --> 01:26:29.143
We fight in their stead.

01:26:36.734 --> 01:26:38.986
[piano plays softly]

01:26:39.445 --> 01:26:40.821
Is that a piano?

01:26:43.657 --> 01:26:44.742
Braddock's.

01:26:45.409 --> 01:26:48.078
Hauled it all the way
from Alexandria.

01:26:48.203 --> 01:26:49.163
I'm sorry.

01:26:49.288 --> 01:26:52.958
We're cuttin' a road all the way
through the Ohio territory...

01:26:53.083 --> 01:26:54.710
for a piano.

01:26:59.548 --> 01:27:00.841
God help us.

01:27:01.634 --> 01:27:04.011
[George] One. Two.
Three!

01:27:04.136 --> 01:27:05.596
[men groan with effort]

01:27:06.972 --> 01:27:08.140
- [David] Tucker!
- [Henry] Watch your feet.

01:27:08.390 --> 01:27:09.433
[David] It's gettin'
stuck.

01:27:09.558 --> 01:27:11.060
[overlapping chatter]

01:27:11.518 --> 01:27:12.686
[David] Keep goin'!

01:27:13.145 --> 01:27:14.188
[men groan with
effort]

01:27:14.313 --> 01:27:15.272
[George groans in
pain]

01:27:15.397 --> 01:27:16.357
[George coughs]

01:27:16.482 --> 01:27:18.025
Hey, George.
You sure you're all right?

01:27:19.276 --> 01:27:20.069
I'm fine.

01:27:20.194 --> 01:27:21.236
Keep pushing, keep pushing.

01:27:21.362 --> 01:27:22.196
We're nearly there.

01:27:22.321 --> 01:27:24.448
[Braddock] You will acquaint
Mr. Hunter

01:27:24.573 --> 01:27:27.201
that His Majesty’s service
requires the further sum

01:27:27.326 --> 01:27:29.912
of 10,000 pounds sterling.

01:27:31.038 --> 01:27:34.541
[Braddock] How else are we to
deal with the lack of roads

01:27:34.792 --> 01:27:38.337
in a wilderness
that is proven formidable?

01:27:39.004 --> 01:27:40.089
Did you get that?

01:27:40.214 --> 01:27:41.340
Yes, Your Excellency.

01:27:41.465 --> 01:27:42.841
Now, where was I?

01:27:45.010 --> 01:27:47.471
The siege had been the
longest and the bloodiest...

01:27:47.596 --> 01:27:48.389
[warbling voices]

01:27:48.514 --> 01:27:49.306
Washington?

01:27:49.431 --> 01:27:51.308
oh man, you’re pale as a ghost.

01:27:54.395 --> 01:27:55.688
[Braddock muffled]
Washington.

01:27:56.563 --> 01:27:57.690
[Braddock]
Washington!

01:27:57.815 --> 01:27:58.691
Deliver the dispatch!

01:27:58.816 --> 01:28:02.861
Sorry, Your Excellency, I was
lost in your story.

01:28:11.161 --> 01:28:12.037
Gist!

01:28:18.544 --> 01:28:19.670
[Gage] How is he?

01:28:22.715 --> 01:28:24.049
Dysentery.

01:28:24.425 --> 01:28:26.135
His case is very severe.

01:28:26.760 --> 01:28:29.054
High fever,
terrible nightmares.

01:28:29.179 --> 01:28:30.389
He calls out names.

01:28:30.514 --> 01:28:32.391
How long will he be down?

01:28:32.516 --> 01:28:36.729
Days, a week, forever.

01:28:37.396 --> 01:28:38.647
Forever?

01:28:38.856 --> 01:28:40.774
He'll survive, won't he?

01:28:48.907 --> 01:28:49.908
Washington.

01:28:53.537 --> 01:28:54.496
You're awake.

01:28:55.080 --> 01:28:56.040
Where are we?

01:28:56.457 --> 01:28:58.709
Five miles south of the river,
past the great meadows,

01:28:58.834 --> 01:28:59.960
where you fought.

01:29:00.085 --> 01:29:01.628
At Necessity. Yes.

01:29:01.754 --> 01:29:05.758
I’ve been tasked with a command
of a flying column and 900 men.

01:29:05.883 --> 01:29:07.718
We cross the
Monongahela River tomorrow.

01:29:07.843 --> 01:29:10.429
The next day we
reach Fort Duquesne.

01:29:10.763 --> 01:29:12.139
You should rest.

01:29:12.306 --> 01:29:13.265
No!

01:29:20.105 --> 01:29:21.398
Look to the trees.

01:29:22.357 --> 01:29:25.277
This is a new world,
treat it that way.

01:29:25.402 --> 01:29:27.154
Do you not think me
up to the task?

01:29:27.279 --> 01:29:28.572
You weren't there.

01:29:29.782 --> 01:29:31.575
I question the strategy.

01:29:32.159 --> 01:29:33.285
[Nurse] That's enough.

01:29:33.535 --> 01:29:35.412
Gage, look to the trees.

01:29:36.747 --> 01:29:40.250
I've been preparing
for this all my life, George.

01:29:45.005 --> 01:29:46.048
Courage, man.

01:29:49.468 --> 01:29:50.844
God please help us.

01:29:59.520 --> 01:30:01.980
[dramatic music]

01:30:06.568 --> 01:30:07.945
Hold the advance.

01:30:08.070 --> 01:30:09.780
[Soldier] Hold the
advance!

01:30:10.072 --> 01:30:11.657
[Soldier] Hold the
advance.

01:30:16.078 --> 01:30:17.913
[eerie music plays]

01:30:19.957 --> 01:30:21.333
Advance the column.

01:30:21.667 --> 01:30:23.168
[Soldier] Advance the
column.

01:30:34.138 --> 01:30:36.390
[eerie music continues]

01:30:43.272 --> 01:30:44.481
[bird call sound]

01:30:44.857 --> 01:30:45.899
Halt!

01:30:46.150 --> 01:30:47.234
[Soldier] Halt.

01:30:51.321 --> 01:30:54.032
[man] Whoo!

01:30:55.284 --> 01:30:57.536
[overlapping chatter]

01:31:00.205 --> 01:31:01.248
[gunshot]

01:31:02.749 --> 01:31:03.834
Ambush!

01:31:04.084 --> 01:31:05.043
[men yelling]

01:31:05.169 --> 01:31:06.128
[guns cock]

01:31:06.253 --> 01:31:07.671
In line formation.

01:31:09.423 --> 01:31:11.133
[Gage] In line
formation!

01:31:13.844 --> 01:31:14.845
[men whooping]

01:31:14.970 --> 01:31:15.846
Form square!

01:31:16.180 --> 01:31:17.055
Form square!

01:31:17.598 --> 01:31:20.017
Form square,
protect the column!

01:31:20.934 --> 01:31:22.436
[gunshots impacting]

01:31:23.270 --> 01:31:24.813
[men yelling and
whooping]

01:31:33.822 --> 01:31:35.741
Number one section,
number two section.

01:31:35.866 --> 01:31:37.159
In line formation.

01:31:37.868 --> 01:31:41.205
Number one section,
present... fire.

01:31:44.833 --> 01:31:48.212
Number two section,
present... fire.

01:31:48.921 --> 01:31:51.340
Number one section,
number two section.

01:31:51.465 --> 01:31:52.799
To my rear!

01:31:53.383 --> 01:31:54.885
Protect the colors!

01:31:55.636 --> 01:31:56.762
Get 'em to the river.

01:31:56.970 --> 01:31:58.555
- [David] To the river!
- [Henry] To the river!

01:31:58.680 --> 01:32:00.349
[inaudible yelling]

01:32:00.724 --> 01:32:01.725
[Henry] To the river!

01:32:01.850 --> 01:32:03.810
Get 'em to the river.
Come on!

01:32:04.478 --> 01:32:06.021
We'll regroup at the river!

01:32:06.146 --> 01:32:07.898
[cacophony of yelling
and gunfire]

01:32:08.023 --> 01:32:09.066
Retreat!

01:32:09.650 --> 01:32:10.776
[horse neighing]

01:32:11.652 --> 01:32:13.570
[intense drum beats]

01:32:18.116 --> 01:32:20.160
[Braddock] Make ready!
Present...

01:32:21.078 --> 01:32:21.745
Fire!

01:32:22.829 --> 01:32:24.706
[gunfire]

01:32:24.831 --> 01:32:26.375
Build a rank, build a rank!

01:32:26.500 --> 01:32:27.417
Build a line!

01:32:27.876 --> 01:32:28.543
Move forward!

01:32:28.669 --> 01:32:29.628
Move forward!

01:32:30.796 --> 01:32:31.546
[gunfire]

01:32:32.756 --> 01:32:34.216
Build a rank!

01:32:34.549 --> 01:32:35.842
[Braddock] Hold the line!
Hold the line!

01:32:36.677 --> 01:32:38.220
[intense, epic music]

01:32:39.680 --> 01:32:41.181
[gunfire]

01:32:43.100 --> 01:32:44.142
[cannon fire booms]

01:32:53.443 --> 01:32:54.444
[cannon fire booms]

01:32:57.114 --> 01:32:58.448
[gasping]

01:33:04.663 --> 01:33:06.456
[cacophony of
gunfire and yelling]

01:33:06.623 --> 01:33:08.000
[explosion]

01:33:08.125 --> 01:33:09.293
What happened?

01:33:09.876 --> 01:33:10.877
We've been ambushed!

01:33:11.003 --> 01:33:11.837
From where?

01:33:11.962 --> 01:33:12.963
Over the hill!

01:33:14.131 --> 01:33:15.799
[gunfire]

01:33:19.720 --> 01:33:23.181
[sounds muffle,
gasping as ringing starts]

01:33:23.307 --> 01:33:24.641
[grunts with effort]

01:33:28.729 --> 01:33:29.646
[gunfire]

01:33:30.439 --> 01:33:32.107
[cannon fire]

01:33:33.191 --> 01:33:35.235
[epic music]

01:33:42.242 --> 01:33:43.618
I wouldn't bother,
Washington.

01:33:44.202 --> 01:33:45.495
The battle's lost.

01:33:46.580 --> 01:33:47.456
Where's the General?

01:33:47.581 --> 01:33:49.082
Ordered a full retreat.

01:33:49.207 --> 01:33:50.000
And my men?

01:33:50.208 --> 01:33:51.126
You have no men.

01:33:51.251 --> 01:33:52.336
The Virginians.

01:33:53.253 --> 01:33:54.796
They were at the
front of the line.

01:33:54.921 --> 01:33:56.882
It's nearly four
miles from here.

01:33:57.549 --> 01:33:59.760
If you go that way,
you will die.

01:34:00.635 --> 01:34:02.637
You look like death already.

01:34:03.055 --> 01:34:04.264
Listen to me.

01:34:06.266 --> 01:34:07.225
You'll never find them.

01:34:07.351 --> 01:34:09.394
And even if you did,
you'd never make it back.

01:34:10.062 --> 01:34:11.313
[bullet whizzes]

01:34:11.438 --> 01:34:12.439
Washington.

01:34:13.148 --> 01:34:14.107
Washington.

01:34:14.983 --> 01:34:16.109
Come, my friend.

01:34:17.152 --> 01:34:19.237
What could be worth the risk?

01:34:22.574 --> 01:34:24.117
[dramatic stinger]

01:34:24.242 --> 01:34:25.577
My men.

01:34:30.582 --> 01:34:31.958
[epic music]

01:34:36.922 --> 01:34:39.633
[explosions thunder]

01:34:45.430 --> 01:34:46.431
[soldier grunts]

01:34:51.395 --> 01:34:52.521
[cannon booms]

01:34:53.730 --> 01:34:54.731
[groans]

01:34:54.856 --> 01:34:56.149
[epic music continues]

01:35:02.906 --> 01:35:04.241
[Indistinct yelling]

01:35:04.574 --> 01:35:05.826
Where is the General?

01:35:05.951 --> 01:35:07.244
Where is Braddock?

01:35:07.369 --> 01:35:09.162
Hey! Listen to me!

01:35:09.287 --> 01:35:10.747
- [bullet whizzes by]
- [horse neighs]

01:35:11.164 --> 01:35:12.332
[groans]

01:35:13.250 --> 01:35:15.710
Number one section.
Number two section.

01:35:15.836 --> 01:35:17.129
Fix bayonets.

01:35:18.755 --> 01:35:19.881
[cacophony of gunfire
and screams]

01:35:20.006 --> 01:35:21.967
[yelling]

01:35:22.175 --> 01:35:23.343
[indistinct yelling]

01:35:24.845 --> 01:35:25.846
[groans]

01:35:35.730 --> 01:35:37.649
[ominous tones]

01:35:45.615 --> 01:35:47.200
[gunshots crack]

01:35:49.578 --> 01:35:51.329
Where is the General?

01:35:51.496 --> 01:35:52.914
[soldier] He's over
here!

01:35:53.165 --> 01:35:54.207
Over here!

01:35:57.169 --> 01:35:58.086
General.

01:35:58.462 --> 01:35:59.129
General.

01:35:59.463 --> 01:36:01.923
[panting]

01:36:02.340 --> 01:36:03.425
Washington.

01:36:03.967 --> 01:36:04.968
Sir.

01:36:06.052 --> 01:36:07.137
You ordered a retreat?

01:36:07.596 --> 01:36:10.098
I ordered no retreat.

01:36:13.768 --> 01:36:16.354
Rally the men and fall back.

01:36:18.648 --> 01:36:19.316
Wear...

01:36:19.649 --> 01:36:20.358
Wear this.

01:36:20.525 --> 01:36:22.235
They'll know it's mine.

01:36:26.573 --> 01:36:32.162
Take my horse and save
as many as you can.

01:36:34.873 --> 01:36:35.749
Yes, sir.

01:36:37.501 --> 01:36:39.211
I won't let you down.

01:36:40.921 --> 01:36:42.339
[dramatic music]

01:36:44.633 --> 01:36:46.259
Who would have thought?

01:36:48.053 --> 01:36:50.430
[inspiring music]

01:36:52.766 --> 01:36:53.767
Retreat!

01:36:53.892 --> 01:36:55.602
[booming thuds]

01:36:57.646 --> 01:37:00.106
[George] Hold your ground,
there is no retreat.

01:37:00.232 --> 01:37:01.358
This way!

01:37:02.817 --> 01:37:04.236
There is no retreat.

01:37:05.987 --> 01:37:07.781
Fall back! Fall back!

01:37:07.906 --> 01:37:10.617
Hold your ground,
there is no retreat!

01:37:10.825 --> 01:37:12.160
Hold fast!

01:37:15.205 --> 01:37:16.331
Forward!

01:37:18.708 --> 01:37:19.793
On me!

01:37:20.418 --> 01:37:21.419
[Tucker] George!

01:37:22.754 --> 01:37:24.005
Their advance ends here.

01:37:24.130 --> 01:37:25.966
We will hold this line.

01:37:26.258 --> 01:37:27.467
Fire and move!

01:37:28.885 --> 01:37:30.220
Find cover in the trees.

01:37:30.345 --> 01:37:31.721
Fire from the trees.

01:37:31.846 --> 01:37:32.639
Spread out.

01:37:32.806 --> 01:37:33.598
Spread out.

01:37:34.474 --> 01:37:37.602
Men this is our land
and we will fight for it.

01:37:37.727 --> 01:37:38.728
Independent fire.

01:37:38.853 --> 01:37:39.771
Independent fire!

01:37:41.606 --> 01:37:42.607
George!

01:37:43.066 --> 01:37:43.733
Tucker.

01:37:44.568 --> 01:37:45.485
Where are the others?

01:37:45.610 --> 01:37:46.653
Where's David?
Where's Henry?

01:37:46.778 --> 01:37:48.321
By the river, surrounded.

01:37:48.446 --> 01:37:50.115
If they're still alive.

01:37:50.240 --> 01:37:51.658
I'm going to try to reach them.

01:37:51.783 --> 01:37:53.994
Tucker, rally as many as you can
and move to the river.

01:37:54.119 --> 01:37:55.453
Wait for my signal.

01:37:55.579 --> 01:37:57.038
I won't let you down, sir.

01:37:57.163 --> 01:37:58.248
I'm no officer.

01:37:58.415 --> 01:38:00.333
You are the only leader
on this field.

01:38:00.458 --> 01:38:01.668
Buy me some time.

01:38:03.878 --> 01:38:04.546
You there...

01:38:04.671 --> 01:38:06.339
You, you, and you, follow
me. We'll get to the river.

01:38:06.464 --> 01:38:07.424
On my command!

01:38:07.549 --> 01:38:08.466
[groans]

01:38:08.592 --> 01:38:09.634
Make ready.

01:38:10.343 --> 01:38:11.344
[horse neighs]

01:38:11.469 --> 01:38:12.554
Fire!

01:38:12.929 --> 01:38:14.639
[gunshots ring out]

01:38:17.767 --> 01:38:20.145
[loud booming thuds]

01:38:21.896 --> 01:38:23.398
[men yelling]

01:38:24.774 --> 01:38:25.650
[gunshot]

01:38:26.693 --> 01:38:29.070
Argh! You damn British guns.

01:38:30.614 --> 01:38:31.615
[Sam whimpers]

01:38:31.740 --> 01:38:33.617
No, No, No. Sam,
stay with me, son.

01:38:33.742 --> 01:38:35.952
Brits left us here to die.

01:38:36.202 --> 01:38:37.704
You sound surprised.

01:38:38.371 --> 01:38:39.372
[Charles] Sam...

01:38:42.876 --> 01:38:44.085
[Henry] How many
rounds left?

01:38:44.252 --> 01:38:46.546
My gun doesn't even work, Henry.

01:38:47.380 --> 01:38:48.590
[gunshots ringing]

01:38:49.674 --> 01:38:50.884
Check for powder.

01:38:54.512 --> 01:38:55.388
[horse neighs]

01:38:56.222 --> 01:38:57.390
Henry, look.

01:38:58.391 --> 01:38:59.643
[Henry] Is that...

01:38:59.934 --> 01:39:01.603
[epic music]

01:39:04.939 --> 01:39:06.232
It's Washington.

01:39:06.358 --> 01:39:07.651
Man's a damn fool.

01:39:11.905 --> 01:39:12.822
[grunts]

01:39:12.947 --> 01:39:14.866
Come on.

01:39:14.991 --> 01:39:16.159
[gunshots]

01:39:16.284 --> 01:39:17.535
[grunting]

01:39:22.624 --> 01:39:24.000
[yelling]

01:39:24.668 --> 01:39:25.919
[gunshot]

01:39:37.514 --> 01:39:38.556
- They're behind us.
- [David] Huh?

01:39:38.807 --> 01:39:40.475
They flanked you
from the right side.

01:39:40.600 --> 01:39:41.726
Well, what do we do?

01:39:41.851 --> 01:39:42.519
We fight.

01:39:42.644 --> 01:39:44.229
We're all out of power.

01:39:45.563 --> 01:39:47.190
Has anybody got powder?

01:39:47.399 --> 01:39:48.066
Who has powder?

01:39:48.191 --> 01:39:49.275
Here! I got it!

01:39:51.695 --> 01:39:52.821
Let's make 'em pay.

01:39:54.114 --> 01:39:55.740
Reload every weapon
you can find.

01:39:55.865 --> 01:39:57.992
Men of Virginia,
reload your weapons.

01:39:58.118 --> 01:39:59.703
To the right, follow me.

01:39:59.828 --> 01:40:02.163
Keep that powder on you
and keep it dry.

01:40:02.372 --> 01:40:04.374
Let's go, let's go!
Let's give'em hell.

01:40:05.417 --> 01:40:06.751
[David] Keep your
head down, Henry.

01:40:07.001 --> 01:40:07.961
[grunting]

01:40:08.086 --> 01:40:10.338
[George] Virginians, take
cover along the berm!

01:40:12.465 --> 01:40:14.342
Keep your heads down.

01:40:14.801 --> 01:40:16.636
[cacophony of gunfire
and cannon explosions]

01:40:21.933 --> 01:40:24.102
Reload your muskets.

01:40:26.521 --> 01:40:28.732
Ahh... you bastard.

01:40:29.399 --> 01:40:30.483
Make ready.

01:40:31.818 --> 01:40:32.902
Ready?

01:40:33.027 --> 01:40:34.112
Present arms!

01:40:36.489 --> 01:40:37.532
Fire!

01:40:39.284 --> 01:40:40.160
Second rank.

01:40:43.830 --> 01:40:44.622
Make ready.

01:40:45.457 --> 01:40:46.374
Present arms.

01:40:47.250 --> 01:40:48.251
Fire!

01:40:52.213 --> 01:40:55.383
On my signal, take the men
as fast as you can to the right.

01:40:55.508 --> 01:40:57.302
What are you going to do?

01:41:00.180 --> 01:41:01.556
George.

01:41:02.182 --> 01:41:03.600
[epic music]

01:41:08.104 --> 01:41:09.355
[gunfire]

01:41:16.529 --> 01:41:18.406
He's makin’ himself a target.

01:41:20.700 --> 01:41:22.494
[epic music]

01:41:25.789 --> 01:41:27.165
[speaking Seneca]

01:41:31.753 --> 01:41:33.129
[bullets whizzing]

01:41:42.722 --> 01:41:43.640
Now!

01:41:43.932 --> 01:41:44.766
Now!

01:41:46.935 --> 01:41:47.936
[Tucker] Present!

01:41:49.229 --> 01:41:50.188
Fire!

01:41:52.398 --> 01:41:53.358
[Tucker] Freedom!

01:41:53.483 --> 01:41:55.109
Independent fire!

01:41:55.735 --> 01:41:58.238
[muskets cracking]

01:41:58.530 --> 01:42:00.865
Men of Virginia, to the right!

01:42:01.783 --> 01:42:03.159
[George] Go! Go!

01:42:03.743 --> 01:42:05.245
[triumphant music]

01:42:08.164 --> 01:42:09.791
[explosions thunder]

01:42:18.424 --> 01:42:20.635
[dramatic music
intensifies]

01:42:39.279 --> 01:42:40.947
[distant gunshots]

01:42:48.413 --> 01:42:51.833
Only tend to the ones who
you can see breathing.

01:42:51.958 --> 01:42:52.876
What is that?

01:42:55.795 --> 01:42:58.756
[triumphant music]

01:43:00.633 --> 01:43:01.926
[birds chirping]

01:43:25.783 --> 01:43:27.911
[triumphant music continues]

01:43:47.972 --> 01:43:49.515
What's wrong, sir?

01:43:50.516 --> 01:43:51.726
Seen a ghost?

01:43:52.310 --> 01:43:54.020
[triumphant music]

01:44:04.072 --> 01:44:04.906
There was no order.

01:44:05.031 --> 01:44:05.698
What?

01:44:05.949 --> 01:44:07.033
To retreat.

01:44:12.705 --> 01:44:14.791
The battle was lost, George.

01:44:15.750 --> 01:44:18.836
I see no point in
joining him in the grave.

01:44:19.837 --> 01:44:22.006
Whose land is this, anyway?

01:44:22.966 --> 01:44:24.175
It's our land.

01:44:24.634 --> 01:44:26.886
Well, my land is an ocean away.

01:44:34.519 --> 01:44:37.522
See, that is the
difference between us.

01:44:45.655 --> 01:44:46.781
You all right?

01:44:46.948 --> 01:44:48.324
How are the others?

01:44:48.741 --> 01:44:49.909
We lost a lot of men.

01:44:50.034 --> 01:44:51.035
How many?

01:44:52.161 --> 01:44:53.329
Hundreds.

01:44:54.789 --> 01:44:56.624
[solemn music]

01:45:04.382 --> 01:45:09.137
Thank you for
coming back for us.

01:45:15.184 --> 01:45:18.688
Major Washington, the Half-King.

01:45:24.736 --> 01:45:26.863
[ominous music]

01:45:43.296 --> 01:45:44.922
So, now you fight
for the French?

01:45:45.631 --> 01:45:48.551
I no longer fight wars
that are not my own.

01:45:48.676 --> 01:45:50.261
Then why are you here?

01:45:50.762 --> 01:45:51.637
To find you.

01:45:53.514 --> 01:45:54.515
Follow me.

01:45:56.392 --> 01:45:57.769
[ominous music
builds]

01:46:04.442 --> 01:46:05.860
[speaking Native language]

01:46:06.736 --> 01:46:09.155
He wants to know who you are.

01:46:10.865 --> 01:46:11.824
Why?

01:46:13.868 --> 01:46:15.495
[speaking Native language]

01:46:21.042 --> 01:46:23.878
I ordered my
warriors to shoot you.

01:46:24.337 --> 01:46:25.588
All of them.

01:46:27.215 --> 01:46:28.716
My men never miss.

01:46:29.842 --> 01:46:32.637
[speaking Native language]

01:46:41.187 --> 01:46:44.524
Our people have a legend.

01:46:45.316 --> 01:46:48.402
A spirit of protection that
shields those chosen,

01:46:48.528 --> 01:46:50.404
those who walk in destiny.

01:46:50.571 --> 01:46:54.075
[speaking Native language]

01:46:54.575 --> 01:46:56.035
Creator chose you.

01:46:56.494 --> 01:46:58.663
You've been
shielded by the spirit.

01:46:58.788 --> 01:47:01.833
[speaking Native language]

01:47:01.958 --> 01:47:03.084
So, I ask again.

01:47:03.334 --> 01:47:04.752
What are you called?

01:47:07.880 --> 01:47:09.966
My name is George Washington.

01:47:12.093 --> 01:47:13.553
[speaking Native language]

01:47:16.389 --> 01:47:18.266
I will remember this name.

01:47:21.978 --> 01:47:24.272
[Dinwiddie] Are those bullet
holes in your jacket?

01:47:24.564 --> 01:47:25.273
Apologies,

01:47:25.439 --> 01:47:26.691
sir, this is
the only uniform I own--

01:47:26.816 --> 01:47:28.526
You misunderstand my statement.

01:47:28.651 --> 01:47:29.569
And your hat?

01:47:30.194 --> 01:47:32.196
Yes, it's the
only one I own as well.

01:47:32.321 --> 01:47:33.364
The militia is in general--

01:47:33.489 --> 01:47:36.075
It also has a
bullet hole in it.

01:47:39.203 --> 01:47:40.788
How are you alive?

01:47:42.373 --> 01:47:44.208
A divine hand, perhaps.

01:47:44.417 --> 01:47:45.334
Perhaps.

01:47:45.751 --> 01:47:46.878
That says maybe.

01:47:47.837 --> 01:47:50.590
But you are
the man of the hour.

01:47:50.840 --> 01:47:51.924
That's certain.

01:47:52.216 --> 01:47:54.302
Your journals to the council,
they've been published

01:47:54.427 --> 01:47:55.595
and have made
you quite well known.

01:47:55.720 --> 01:47:57.346
They've even awakened London

01:47:57.471 --> 01:47:59.515
to the situation our
colonies now face.

01:47:59.640 --> 01:48:01.350
The way you
describe the frontier

01:48:01.475 --> 01:48:04.770
has sparked the
imagination of many.

01:48:06.564 --> 01:48:10.735
And, um... to your
recent actions,

01:48:12.612 --> 01:48:15.615
Mr. Washington's
exemplary courage

01:48:15.740 --> 01:48:19.160
was on full display as he evaded
many attacks on his person

01:48:19.285 --> 01:48:22.705
while he felled
Indian and French enemies alike.

01:48:22.830 --> 01:48:26.834
He also selflessly
rescued hundreds of his men

01:48:26.959 --> 01:48:28.753
during a most
impressive retreat,

01:48:28.878 --> 01:48:31.672
during which he continued
to battle the enemy with fervor,

01:48:31.797 --> 01:48:33.633
despite his infirm condition.

01:48:33.758 --> 01:48:35.384
Well, we were defeated.

01:48:35.843 --> 01:48:38.638
Sir, 450 lives lost,
another 500 wounded.

01:48:38.763 --> 01:48:39.764
But you have won.

01:48:40.598 --> 01:48:42.225
Because you endured.

01:48:43.309 --> 01:48:45.228
For most, failure is the end.

01:48:45.353 --> 01:48:48.356
For you, it seems
only to be the beginning.

01:48:48.481 --> 01:48:51.275
And since
leadership is the problem,

01:48:53.736 --> 01:48:57.406
I'm going to give you
the opportunity to answer.

01:48:57.740 --> 01:48:59.033
A second chance.

01:49:01.118 --> 01:49:02.995
We're forming
a Virginia regiment,

01:49:03.120 --> 01:49:05.289
1500 men, first of
its kind in the colonies,

01:49:05.414 --> 01:49:06.749
and want you to lead it.

01:49:06.874 --> 01:49:08.542
I'm reinstating your
rank as Colonel

01:49:08.668 --> 01:49:10.044
in the Virginia Regiment.

01:49:10.169 --> 01:49:12.046
And Commander
in Chief of all forces

01:49:12.171 --> 01:49:15.174
raised in defense
of His Majesty's colony.

01:49:15.758 --> 01:49:18.970
Do you accept
this great honor?

01:49:21.806 --> 01:49:23.933
Yes, sir. I do.

01:49:24.183 --> 01:49:25.101
Well then.

01:49:25.518 --> 01:49:26.644
We have much to discuss.

01:49:26.769 --> 01:49:28.938
I have... but one request.

01:49:29.981 --> 01:49:33.442
Washington, if you ask for equal
pay or a royal commission--

01:49:33.567 --> 01:49:34.402
No, sir.

01:49:35.736 --> 01:49:38.322
I would like to
discuss the uniform.

01:49:43.411 --> 01:49:44.412
Fall in!

01:50:08.227 --> 01:50:10.438
Form up on Colonel Washington!

01:50:15.151 --> 01:50:17.069
I am not a British officer.

01:50:20.072 --> 01:50:22.533
I am not a
gentleman of England.

01:50:24.410 --> 01:50:27.913
I have no title,
no royal commission.

01:50:30.583 --> 01:50:32.710
But what I do have is you.

01:50:34.754 --> 01:50:35.838
All of you.

01:50:38.632 --> 01:50:40.092
I am a Virginian.

01:50:43.012 --> 01:50:45.598
And it is my
honor to serve you.

01:50:46.557 --> 01:50:48.017
To Virginia!

01:50:48.225 --> 01:50:49.560
[men] To Virginia!

01:50:49.769 --> 01:50:51.520
[men yell and cheer]

01:51:02.656 --> 01:51:04.075
To Virginia.

01:51:12.416 --> 01:51:14.126
[dramatic music]

01:51:55.292 --> 01:51:58.003
[dramatic music]

01:52:22.736 --> 01:52:23.946
Thank you
for being here tonight.

01:52:24.280 --> 01:52:25.489
You're not
just watching a film,

01:52:25.865 --> 01:52:27.074
you're helping launch a movement

01:52:27.700 --> 01:52:29.535
because the ideals
at the heart of this country

01:52:30.035 --> 01:52:30.744
still matter.

01:52:31.036 --> 01:52:32.705
We believe the story
of George Washington,

01:52:33.372 --> 01:52:36.792
of sacrifice, courage,
humility, perseverance,

01:52:36.917 --> 01:52:38.461
and faith still matters.

01:52:39.253 --> 01:52:41.589
Freedom matters,
virtue matters.

01:52:42.047 --> 01:52:44.383
The belief that
liberty is worth fighting for,

01:52:45.593 --> 01:52:46.594
that still matters.

01:52:47.136 --> 01:52:49.597
So we are inviting
you tonight to Pay it Forward

01:52:49.763 --> 01:52:51.807
because when you do,
you give countless families

01:52:51.932 --> 01:52:53.225
the chance to see
Young Washington,

01:52:53.517 --> 01:52:55.394
and with your help,
Young Washington

01:52:55.603 --> 01:52:57.897
can be America's
number one movie.

01:52:58.731 --> 01:53:01.942
On the 250th anniversary
of our nation's birth,

01:53:02.610 --> 01:53:04.445
we can send a
message loud and clear

01:53:04.570 --> 01:53:08.282
that America, and founding
principles that shaped her,

01:53:09.116 --> 01:53:10.326
are still worth fighting for.

01:53:11.410 --> 01:53:12.661
Thank you so
much for your help.

01:53:13.913 --> 01:53:15.956
[dramatic music]

01:54:20.354 --> 01:54:22.356
[dramatic music]